s as an army of mobbers. The Cries will quickly note that numbers have made them survive the harsh desert enviroment for centuries.<br /> <br /> If the renard are the masters of art, the Cries are the masters of loudness in other ways. They spread rumours, call upon any scandal they may find. The stereotypical person on a soap box. They might be considered similar to ratkin, but the Cries are hardly wyld-mad, they just like to make their news known.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I love this! I've always hated how limited they were geographically. After the Ananasi the foxes are my favourites ^-^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T08:35:01-08:00","id":1058425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1058388#post1058388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd let there be western, African and arctic Kitsune. Many countries have their own fox tales so why not take advantage of that? I liked the idea that European Kitsune like to blend in with the nobles and the wealthy to further their goals (the Roko will sometimes pose as pets) to the point that Prince Harry is one of them. To explain this would be that Bai Mianxi and her love had many children and a number of them went out into the world when they grew-up.<br /> <br /> I'd definitely get rid of the dead parent curse and have the Kitsune be very fertile almost to fault. I'd also have them be one of the few Fera that has no real problems with the Garou since they weren't around during the War of the Rage and Shame. The arctic marble fox would be their attempt to create a new breed of Kitsune to help them out and so far it's been fairly successful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going into other breeds...<br /> <br /> There are 3 European lynxes, and 4 African wildcats. There's no reason to make Ceilican and Bubasti fictional breeds. I'd actually bolster both of their numbers (perhaps, like Naga, having been in hiding.) I'd also include some more on South American Qualmi. <br /> <br /> I'd also split the Bastet into 2 effective (though heavily symbiotic) Breeds (sharing language and a significant amount of culture and gifts). Big cat/warrior tribes and small cat/mystic tribes, with a big sidebar for Pumonca explaining why they are on whichever side they might fall. I would personally say spiritually warrior despite genetic small cat. Also, a bit about the fall of the White Howlers, as the betrayal of Lion happening to coincide with lions being exterminated north of the Mediterranean deserves more of a note than it's gotten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T08:43:55-08:00","id":1058428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1058412#post1058412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on current genetic studies, I'd make the nuwisha another tribe of Garou. They betrayed the Garou during the war of rage and sided with the Fera.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, at times I feel sorry for the writers because of stuff like this. For some reason, WtA attracts people who love doing research on animals, and so stuff like the coywolves of America and Chernobyl's wolf population tend to pop up in discussion.<br /> <br /> Then again, I think it keeps the writing on point, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T09:04:31-08:00","id":1058437,"title":"","content":"I'd keep the setting basically as it was in the first corebooks before it was developed further. I'd retain those things I'd like and jettison those that I don't in later material like the various tribebooks and other sourcebooks. Basically it would be a big editing job with some additional points thrown in.<br /> <br /> 1) I'd incorporate more real world folklore, literary, and cinematic werewolf legends and tropes to strengthen the Garou to their inspiration. You only need some appropriate merits, fetishes, and additional rules specific to it (like wolfsbane). I'd also make sure that sourcebooks with Garou characters referenced those things so you could see them in canonical characters.<br /> <br /> 2) Bunyip aren't Garou. They are just another group of Fera that the Garou slaughtered. Weremarsupials are fine, but they are not werewolves.<br /> <br /> 3) Glass Walkers would be a tribe that only was created in relatively modern times (say in the past few hundred years). There were previous attempts of Garou to create a more Weaver friendly tribe, but they always failed - and their prospective totems would be much more appropriate to the concept of the Weaver in earlier times - honeybees, ants, perhaps even spiders.<br /> <br /> 4) Stargazers aren't the Asian tribe, although its fine for them to have most of their numbers in the Himalayas and Tibet. They are the mountain wolves. Modern days concepts of multiculturalism make no sense for the Garou and Fera given their history and connection to Ancestors.<br /> <br /> 5) Crinos form does not have opposable thumbs. If you want your werewolf to carry and fire guns, stay in homid or glabro.<br /> <br /> 6) Glabro would be more apparently the old Lon Chaney wolfman form, not some bestial looking neanderthal.<br /> <br /> 7) Less cartoonish opponents - PENTEX badly needs to be rewritten, and more thought is needed for opponents of the Garou before the time of industrial pollution. I'd add various factions/types of Fomori who could act as long term opponents on their own in order to diversify the foes the Garou fought, and bring in rival Wyrm groups that would fight each other as well as the Garou.<br /> <br /> 8) When doing totems for the tribes, do much more reading on real world legend and myth for them when the tribebooks were rewritten.<br /> <br /> 9) In the corebook, I'd add at least 3-4 more new totems for each type (Honor, Glory, Wisdom).and better write the bans for each of them.<br /> <br /> 10) I'd make the Wyrm infestation within the tribes more prominent in order to create more intrigue within the Garou. Eating man flesh would give Gnosis and powers, but corrupt those who did it. The Maneaters and similar human eating camps would be a big opponent within the Garou Nation. Typhon as a Wyrm spirit would be seducing ever more Garou to his service.<br /> <br /> 11) I would not make Weaver spirits too much like spiders or have webs in the Umbra. Calling them &quot;spiders&quot; would simply be a function of their general form, and webs wouldn't be &quot;webs&quot;. These aren't animal spirits, but clearly something else. Some other design aesthetic is needed to showcase artifice. A lot more work needs to be done on the Weaver.<br /> <br /> 12) All the tribes would be redeveloped with the less wise portions of their tribebooks edited out and all new camps/factions done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T09:15:55-08:00","id":1058440,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> I'd say that Opposable Thumbs in Crinos should be a 5 point merit, and the gift that sizes up guns to match your Crinos should die in a big big pit of silver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T09:25:37-08:00","id":1058444,"title":"","content":"Well, there are other Asian tribes of Garou (and many of them are part of the Beast Courts). From what I understand, there are Asian Bone Gnawers, Asian Children of Gaia, Asian Glass Walkers (other than the Boli Zousizhe), Asian Red Talons, Asian Shadow Lords (other than the Hakkan), Asian Silent Striders, Asian Silver Fangs, and Asian Uktenu. The only specifically European Tribes are Fianna and Get of Fenris just like the Croatan and the Wendigo were the only specifically Native American Tribes and the Bunyip were the only specifically Australian Tribe.<br /> <br /> I agree that there should have been marsupial Fera, I just think that the Bunyip should have been were-dingos rather than were-marsupials. The were-marsupials would have likely been related to the marsupial carnivore species. Alternatively, the Bunyip could have been a term for a loose alliance of different native Fera (Corax, Garou, Mokole, Marsupia, etcl) that would have protected Australia until the European invasion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T09:59:12-08:00","id":1058452,"title":"","content":"I'd keep crinos opposable thumbs but make it so claws make using tools in Crinos difficult. You could trim your claws to use tools better, but you lose the damage bonus and no self respecting Garou would clip his claws like a dog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T10:24:38-08:00","id":1058465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1058444#post1058444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there are other Asian tribes of Garou (and many of them are part of the Beast Courts). From what I understand, there are Asian Bone Gnawers, Asian Children of Gaia, Asian Glass Walkers (other than the Boli Zousizhe), Asian Red Talons, Asian Shadow Lords (other than the Hakkan), Asian Silent Striders, Asian Silver Fangs, and Asian Uktenu. The only specifically European Tribes are Fianna and Get of Fenris just like the Croatan and the Wendigo were the only specifically Native American Tribes and the Bunyip were the only specifically Australian Tribe.<br /> <br /> I agree that there should have been marsupial Fera, I just think that the Bunyip should have been were-dingos rather than were-marsupials. The were-marsupials would have likely been related to the marsupial carnivore species. Alternatively, the Bunyip could have been a term for a loose alliance of different native Fera (Corax, Garou, Mokole, Marsupia, etcl) that would have protected Australia until the European invasion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that Dingos weren't native to Australia, and are one of the reasons the thylacine went exinct on mainland Australia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T00:28:14-08:00","id":1058810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1058452#post1058452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd keep crinos opposable thumbs but make it so claws make using tools in Crinos difficult. You could trim your claws to use tools better, but you lose the damage bonus and no self respecting Garou would clip his claws like a dog.</div> </div> </div> </div>This might be a fun time to mention Dog-Tagging; the Sabbat game where they try and put a tag on a Lupine's ear, before running away very very fast. Suffice it to say, Packs who try this often end up dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T15:09:58-08:00","id":1059226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1058810#post1058810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This might be a fun time to mention Dog-Tagging; the Sabbat game where they try and put a tag on a Lupine's ear, before running away very very fast. Suffice it to say, Packs who try this often end up dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all fun and games until a Sabbat pack gets mauled by a pissed-off werewolf. <br /> <br /> Oh wait, it's even more fun and games when that happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T15:17:47-08:00","id":1059231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1059226#post1059226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's all fun and games until a Sabbat pack gets mauled by a pissed-off werewolf.<br /> <br /> Oh wait, it's even more fun and games when that happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm imagining the righteous fury of a Garou who got forced into a dog tag or a collar of some kind.<br /> <br /> Speaking of making Garou Frenzy:<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, if it isn't Twilight Princess&quot;<br /> &quot;Sorry, but I just don't have time for you right now [stereotyptical dog game like Spot]&quot;<br /> &quot;I'd better kill you before you Imprint on any infants, Jacob.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T15:24:43-08:00","id":1059234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1059231#post1059231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm imagining the righteous fury of a Garou who got forced into a dog tag or a collar of some kind.<br /> <br /> Speaking of making Garou Frenzy:<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, if it isn't Twilight Princess&quot;<br /> &quot;Sorry, but I just don't have time for you right now [stereotyptical dog game like Spot]&quot;<br /> &quot;I'd better kill you before you Imprint on any infants, Jacob.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>None of those are likely to make anyone frenzy unless they're a methed-up Mars Misdsky Ahroun, but the third is a killing offence even so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T15:54:57-08:00","id":1059248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1058253#post1058253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My change would be so big it really wouldn't be recognizable as W:tA anymore\u2014werewolves are the result of a monstrous curse (or rather a number of somewhat similar curses and mystical practices) rather than a hybrid species of spiritually appointed eco-warriors. Being one <i>can</i> be inherited, but most people become werewolves by being bitten, and have no supernatural knowledge or background until that happens. The pack would be the primary social unit, with no septs or Tribes and no Garou Nation. Differences based on the origin of one's particular curse would take the place of Breed and Tribe\u2014you'd have werewolves descended by blood or infection from Lycaon, the \u00dalfhednar, Vseslav of Polotsk, Gilles de Rais<i>, </i>Asena the blue-maned wolf, the Navajo skinwalkers, etc. They wouldn't have any overarching purpose or mission, just individual goals and those of like-minded individuals who band together. Being supernatural creatures werewolves would still be aware of and able to interact with spirits, but rather than their own made-up shamanistic mythology it'd be the spirits of various existing cultures\u2014ghosts, most commonly, and then woodland spirits, demons, and figures out of world religions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would do something like it... Perhaps with a few adjustments to make it interesting. Maybe a division between two larger groups with oposite goals, just like in Werewolf the Forsaken, where the Forsaken fight constantly against the Pure tribes.<br /> <br /> We could have the playable faction, those Werewolves that try to protect this world, by keeping the spirits away, and the faction that wishes to unleash the spirits in the world, destroying civilization and bringing the world back to its natural original state.<br /> <br /> A metaphor for the battle of civilization versus barbarism<br /> <br /> Oh, and beyond those two, those who sold their souls to the demons, of course...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T15:56:31-08:00","id":1059251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1059234#post1059234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> None of those are likely to make anyone frenzy unless they're a methed-up Mars Misdsky Ahroun, but the third is a killing offence even so.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>My Giovanni looks to the camera moments before her decapitation</i><br /> <br /> &quot;Worth it.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T15:58:15-08:00","id":1059253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1058253#post1058253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My change would be so big it really wouldn't be recognizable as W:tA anymore\u2014werewolves are the result of a monstrous curse (or rather a number of somewhat similar curses and mystical practices) rather than a hybrid species of spiritually appointed eco-warriors. Being one <i>can</i> be inherited, but most people become werewolves by being bitten, and have no supernatural knowledge or background until that happens. The pack would be the primary social unit, with no septs or Tribes and no Garou Nation. Differences based on the origin of one's particular curse would take the place of Breed and Tribe\u2014you'd have werewolves descended by blood or infection from Lycaon, the \u00dalfhednar, Vseslav of Polotsk, Gilles de Rais<i>, </i>Asena the blue-maned wolf, the Navajo skinwalkers, etc. They wouldn't have any overarching purpose or mission, just individual goals and those of like-minded individuals who band together. Being supernatural creatures werewolves would still be aware of and able to interact with spirits, but rather than their own made-up shamanistic mythology it'd be the spirits of various existing cultures\u2014ghosts, most commonly, and then woodland spirits, demons, and figures out of world religions.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is... a pretty huge change. I mean my personal alternative canon (Lilith, mother of monsters, made the Changing Breeds) is pretty extreme, but it only changes the origins, not the way things are now if you see what I mean (although it does make Spirits inherently deceptive).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T17:06:57-08:00","id":1059280,"title":"","content":"You see the crux of why I never got into Werewolf like I did several of White Wolf's other games. I've been a big fan of werewolf movies and fiction since long before V:tM was a gleam in Mark Rein\u2022Hagen's eye, and the nature of lycanthropy as a curse that subjects Man to inner and outer savagery that may destroy all he holds dear is what I consider to be the essential core of the premise. The whole superheroic furries for Greenpeace/Wicca thing never held any appeal for me. Black Fox's description of his/her Lovecraftean-tinged take on the game is the only example I've ever heard of that might have worked for me using some version of the WW setup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T18:24:14-08:00","id":1059300,"title":"","content":"The one thing I would change in the WtA would be the current status of the Lost Breeds (Fera/Garou). I would reveal that they didn't die off as believed but are now bound into the Umbra instead of the real world. that would mean all those breeds lost during the rage war are found in random locations of the umbra. Now I would add that some could cross back over and attempted to put a foothold back in the world but then some would never be able to return because they would recreate their lost animal kin. This would allow the writers to dig into an Umbra based shifters storyline and maybe even an Umbra based humans who live there naturally. Hey this is the world of darkness anything could happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T18:39:51-08:00","id":1059304,"title":"","content":"Going back a bit...<br /> <br /> I realized that removing opposable thumbs from Crinos make Crinos pointless compared to Hispo. For the most part Hispo's increased Dexterity is superior to Crinos' increased Strength (and Hispo bites are flat out better than Crinos bites anyway).<br /> <br /> Opposable thumbs are pretty much what makes Crinos worth using: you can effectively use tools. Even if you don't like guns in Crinos, that should probably be addressed directly instead of taking away lots of other things as well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T19:06:26-08:00","id":1059310,"title":"","content":"Guns in Crinos are fairly pointless against the type of enemies that Garou expect to fight (especially since a good number of them are on the spiritual plane). In fact, properly scaled bows firing talon arrows would be much more deadly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T19:11:06-08:00","id":1059312,"title":"","content":"Swords aren't though (which require opposable thumbs), and Garou have a tendency to craft Fetish weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T20:15:21-08:00","id":1059325,"title":"","content":"If I tried to fix everything I disliked with Apocalypse I'd basically be writing my own RPG, but that's not really the point of this thread.<br /> <br /> The one change I'm most keen on is making the Black Furies completely, unashamedly open to trans women.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T04:37:07-08:00","id":1059434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1059325#post1059325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I tried to fix everything I disliked with Apocalypse I'd basically be writing my own RPG, but that's not really the point of this thread.<br /> <br /> The one change I'm most keen on is making the Black Furies completely, unashamedly open to trans women.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, Black Furies are a good example of a tribe united by a concept that has so many different shades they often end up arguing with one another about it. And they are, despite their femine focus, one of the more traditional tribes. For as many Furies who would be open to a trans woman, as many would reject them. For being spies, for perceived affront to Gaia or even out of fear of men in a place they consider safe. Though, the idea of switching gender is very respected spiritually, so a lot of Elders would still be open minded about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> But, respecting trans person outright would be more Children of Gaia, Bone Gnawers, Glass Walkers, Stargazers and Uktena to me. Red Talons would not really care about gender things, since their view of sexuality is more mating based than attraction based.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T06:41:30-08:00","id":1059469,"title":"","content":"Well, it depends on whether you are talking about transgendered women or transsexual women. I think that the Red Talons would care about transsexual women (and transsexual men) because they base sexuality on reproduction, and transsexual people are incapable of reproducing. I do not think that they would give a fig either way about transgendered women (or transgendered men) because gender is a human conception.<br /> <br /> I think that the Black Furies are traditional in the semi-mythical Old Ways that predate the patriarchal societies that dominated the agrarian societies of the last five thousand years. The idea of born male Mortals or born male Kinfolk becoming transgendered women or transsexual women would probably be fine with them because it would represent the willing sacrifice of male privilege to embrace the female principles that they treasure, and self-sacrifice is something that Garou admire and respect. They would probably be much less tolerant of born female Mortals or born female Kinfolk becoming transgendered men or transsexual men because it would represent a rejection of the feminine principles that they treasure in order to benefit from the unearned privilege of men.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T08:05:19-08:00","id":1059520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1059434#post1059434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thing is, Black Furies are a good example of a tribe united by a concept that has so many different shades they often end up arguing with one another about it. And they are, despite their femine focus, one of the more traditional tribes. For as many Furies who would be open to a trans woman, as many would reject them. For being spies, for perceived affront to Gaia or even out of fear of men in a place they consider safe. Though, the idea of switching gender is very respected spiritually, so a lot of Elders would still be open minded about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> But, respecting trans person outright would be more Children of Gaia, Bone Gnawers, Glass Walkers, Stargazers and Uktena to me. Red Talons would not really care about gender things, since their view of sexuality is more mating based than attraction based.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, I thought I was in the thread about changing the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T08:37:26-08:00","id":1059538,"title":"","content":"For Furies, I'd change it so Pegasus the Tribal Totem would completely accept a Transwoman. My first instinct is to leave in a lot of the generational conflict in current feminism among the tribe members. More conservative tribe members would see Transwomen as intruders into the tribe. But then I've been a Storyteller for too long. I'm always looking to bring more conflict into the game. <br /> <br /> As a player, I realize sometimes you just don't want to deal with the bullshit you deal with every day. I've had a similar conversation on the Exalted forums about whether there should be more &quot;sexist&quot; cultures in that setting. The Bronze age the game is based on was not kind to women. My response was always &quot;I deal with gender bullshit every day. If I am going to be judged in an RPG, it's going to be because my character is an soul stealing Anathema, not because her sex organs are innies.&quot; WoD is closer to home and deals with a lot of the darker real life issues, but if a player doesn't want to explore an certain area, then I'll drop it from the game. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T08:52:15-08:00","id":1059548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1059520#post1059520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry, I thought I was in the thread about changing the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies, I did not mean to offend you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T12:09:29-08:00","id":1059656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1059538#post1059538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Furies, I'd change it so Pegasus the Tribal Totem would completely accept a Transwoman. My first instinct is to leave in a lot of the generational conflict in current feminism among the tribe members. More conservative tribe members would see Transwomen as intruders into the tribe. But then I've been a Storyteller for too long. I'm always looking to bring more conflict into the game. <br /> <br /> As a player, I realize sometimes you just don't want to deal with the bullshit you deal with every day. I've had a similar conversation on the Exalted forums about whether there should be more &amp;quot;sexist&amp;quot; cultures in that setting. The Bronze age the game is based on was not kind to women. My response was always &amp;quot;I deal with gender bullshit every day. If I am going to be judged in an RPG, it's going to be because my character is an soul stealing Anathema, not because her sex organs are innies.&amp;quot; WoD is closer to home and deals with a lot of the darker real life issues, but if a player doesn't want to explore an certain area, then I'll drop it from the game. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think Garou can't be transgenders... They would simply &quot;heal&quot; it all back right?<br /> <br /> So.... What's the point of all that discussion?<br /> <br /> Or, is it about the viewpoint of Furies towards HUMANS?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T12:39:43-08:00","id":1059679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentSmith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1059656#post1059656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think Garou can't be transgenders... They would simply &quot;heal&quot; it all back right?<br /> <br /> So.... What's the point of all that discussion?<br /> <br /> Or, is it about the viewpoint of Furies towards HUMANS?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They most certainly can be.<br /> <br /> Transsexual might be an issue, however. But...there are ways around that, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T12:54:51-08:00","id":1059693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentSmith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1059656#post1059656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think Garou can't be transgenders... They would simply &quot;heal&quot; it all back right?<br /> <br /> So.... What's the point of all that discussion?<br /> <br /> Or, is it about the viewpoint of Furies towards HUMANS?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not all transgender people go though the reassignment operations.<br /> <br /> There is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread\">a thread in the off topic forum</a> that answers a bunch of questions about Transgender. Reading the posts there do a better job of explaining that I could.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T13:51:44-08:00","id":1059723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentSmith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1059656#post1059656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think Garou can't be transgenders... They would simply &quot;heal&quot; it all back right?<br /> <br /> So.... What's the point of all that discussion?<br /> <br /> Or, is it about the viewpoint of Furies towards HUMANS?</div> </div> </div> </div>Chiming in to agree with the above 2 posts that Garou certainly can be transgendered. To think they can't seems mostly to imply a misunderstanding of what transgender means.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1059693#post1059693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not all transgender people go though the reassignment operations.<br /> <br /> There is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread\">a thread in the off topic forum</a> that answers a bunch of questions about Transgender. Reading the posts there do a better job of explaining that I could.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read that one yet (thanks for the link), but would recommend <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals\">this thread </a>as well, specifically on the topic of trans women and Black Furies. For the most part, the thread linked handles the discussion is a surprisingly adult civilized manner.<br /> <br /> I can certainly see wanting to change the Furies to be wholly accepting instead of just half accepting which is where I think the Tribe falls as written.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T14:03:24-08:00","id":1059731,"title":"","content":"Yes, transgendered people have existed as far back as we have told stories (Achilles was a girl before he was a man and practically every culture has stories about girls who decide to be men).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T15:56:14-08:00","id":1059802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1059731#post1059731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, transgendered people have existed as far back as we have told stories (Achilles was a girl before he was a man and practically every culture has stories about girls who decide to be men).</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus Vikings had at least some concept of non-binary and cross-dressing and swapping genders (even if they were typically used as narrative comedy), and Native Americans had Twin Souls people (which sounds like a Merit or Splat for WoD but whatever) who believed they were men and women, taking on parts of both roles.<br /> <br /> Don't Garou and Fera have a Gift or Rite that makes you swap genders? I know the Ananasi have a gender swap power which makes you look almost the same with/sans testicles/breasts/etc. and with some changes in figure and jawline. It's a good power since it makes Breeding easier, and disguising, and opens the field to people who want to RP transsexual and transgender character concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T16:20:09-08:00","id":1059811,"title":"","content":"Maybe somewhere in the Tribe books, though I am not sure. I imagine though that it would be easy enough to make up a Rite. Here is an attempt.<br /> <br /> Changing the Skin (Level 3 Mystic Rite)<br /> <br /> Changing the Skin allows the target of the Rite to change their biological sex (female, intersex, or male) while retaining any Pure Breed Background. Among the Black Furies, the Rite is offered as a reward to male Garou and male Kinfolk who impress them or inflicted upon female Garou and female Kinfolk who disappoint them. Among the other Tribes, it is used to make Garou and Kinfolk more comfortable in their own skins. The Rite may only be performed during Winter Solstice if used to transform the target into a female and during the Summer Solstice if used to transform the target into a male (either Equinox is suitable to make someone intersex).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T18:00:27-08:00","id":1059851,"title":"","content":"I believe there's a black fury gift that can change your gender.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13049-darthchocolate","name":"Darthchocolate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T18:14:35-08:00","id":1059857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darthchocolate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1059851#post1059851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe there's a black fury gift that can change your gender.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a Rank 1 Gift for that, but I believe those changes are only superficial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T19:01:20-08:00","id":1059875,"title":"","content":"It's doesn't change actually change your gender. It just lets you pass to others.<br /> <br /> For many trans people, a Gift to pass as male or female would be nice, but it doesn't resolve any sort of dysmorphia and doesn't do anything for non-binary individuals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T19:18:34-08:00","id":1059882,"title":"","content":"Their hate to vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T22:05:08-08:00","id":1059935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1059882#post1059882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their hate to vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's something you'd need to approach from a setting setup perspective, because the way the setting is set up, it's a no go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T22:57:19-08:00","id":1059956,"title":"","content":"If you're not running crossover, it's not that hard to redo leeches to get away from the &quot;automatic kill on sight&quot; and make it more nuanced. Through in some spiritual uncertainty, like vampires are some sort of weird &quot;in-flux&quot; possessed who are easily tainted by different Traitic influences so that most vampires fall too much to the Weaver and Wyrm, but some can embody more Wyld, and some can find balance. This sets up vampires to not be directly hated, and some could even be allies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T23:41:40-08:00","id":1059964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1059956#post1059956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're not running crossover, it's not that hard to redo leeches to get away from the &quot;automatic kill on sight&quot; and make it more nuanced. Through in some spiritual uncertainty, like vampires are some sort of weird &quot;in-flux&quot; possessed who are easily tainted by different Traitic influences so that most vampires fall too much to the Weaver and Wyrm, but some can embody more Wyld, and some can find balance. This sets up vampires to not be directly hated, and some could even be allies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Handwaving the 'wrongness' of walking corpses is kind of difficult, but I admit, this has a certain consistency that I find very appealing.<br /> This approach could actually support the 'friendly Gangrel' type Kindred who could feasibly get along with Garou. If you emphasize vampires as more being empty husks yearning to be spiritually fulfilled, rather than simple Fomori, the ones that miraculously avoid Wyrm/Weaver influence could be treated like gorgons or (best case scenario) really weird Kami (I mean, not really, but something similar that doesn't exist in WtA currently).<br /> <br /> Wyld vamps would probably be ill-equipped for dealing with urban Kindred society. If I were approaching it from the VtM viewpoint, I might require them to be on one of the bestial paths, like Feral Heart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T00:36:16-08:00","id":1059978,"title":"","content":"Well, I admit that there's a certain amount of Kuei-jin in what inspired me. The east Asian setting is generally shown as more cross-creature tolerant as long as people are behaving. It's easier to justify tolerating most &quot;vampires&quot; when you have Yang vampires around that deal politely with the spirit Umbra instead of most vampires that deal with spirits being either necromancers or enslavement (and Caern raider) style Thaumaturgists.<br /> <br /> If western vampires are treated more like a curse that &quot;kills you&quot; but also has you possess your own body (which doesn't even directly contradict the metaphysics of VtM) it gets past some of the innate &quot;icky&quot; of walking corpses. Not completely of course, but enough to allow for easier relations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T05:45:53-08:00","id":1060036,"title":"","content":"The only reason the KJ are tolerated by the Beast Courts is because they have a role assigned to them by the Heavens. When the KJ deviate a centimeter from their assigned roles, the Beast Courts destroy them without hesitation. There is no such role for the Kindred, so they are just undead abominations that need to be killed on sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T06:03:47-08:00","id":1060044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1060036#post1060036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only reason the KJ are tolerated by the Beast Courts is because they have a role assigned to them by the Heavens. When the KJ deviate a centimeter from their assigned roles, the Beast Courts destroy them without hesitation. There is no such role for the Kindred, so they are just undead abominations that need to be killed on sight.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Eh Mages generally don't have a roll and its less kill on sight and KJ tend to heavily deviate from the perspective of the Hengeyokai. I would say its more having a shared language and officially a &quot;common&quot; enemy in the Yama Kings along with most other types at least having a concept of the Centepede and it not being a good thing.<br /> <br /> Kindred are just so profoundly ignorant and out of touch with the broader world. Honestly I'm tempted to drop the whole &quot;Wyrm taint from Embrace&quot; and treat them straight up as humans for purposes of wyrm taint, I'd still get the same &quot;spread&quot; but with less &quot;because its icky&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T07:59:42-08:00","id":1060086,"title":"","content":"de centralize pentex<br /> <br /> turn it into numerouws independent companys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T08:04:09-08:00","id":1060089,"title":"","content":"Well, Kindred that have Humanity 7+ or Path of the Feral Heart (and presumably Road of Beast or Path of Harmony) 7+ are not considered of the Wyrm to the senses of the Fera, so they are capable of 'fitting in'. It is just the ones who are immoral, weak-willed, or faint of heart that cause the Fera problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T23:22:04-08:00","id":1060769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1060089#post1060089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Kindred that have Humanity 7+ or Path of the Feral Heart (and presumably Road of Beast or Path of Harmony) 7+ are not considered of the Wyrm to the senses of the Fera, so they are capable of 'fitting in'. It is just the ones who are immoral, weak-willed, or faint of heart that cause the Fera problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, Dark Ages put it as those on a Path that tries to control their condition, it staved off the corruption. If it is a path that embraces the Embrace, it doesn't.<br /> <br /> In the modern era, even if a Sabat member is trying to control, the sect's behavior and tactics draw the taint in regardless, so for them, it doesn't matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T15:37:24-08:00","id":1180904,"title":"","content":"I'd redo the Umbra in a major way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T15:42:27-08:00","id":1180905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1059935#post1059935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's something you'd need to approach from a setting setup perspective, because the way the setting is set up, it's a no go.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's actually a pretty easy change. You just remove the notion that Vampires stink of this supernatural god-being they've never heard of and have nothing to do with. Conflict can still happen a lot, as with Werewolves and Mages, but it it's pretty easy to remove the Gift-ping that gives Werewolves the &quot;kill on sight&quot; default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T15:48:31-08:00","id":1180908,"title":"","content":"- Sense Wyrm is just Sense Bane. It can detect Fomori (since there is a Bane in there), but it doesn't detect unpossessed servants of the Wyrm (including BSDs). Conflicting views about what are and what are not &quot;of the Wyrm&quot; permeates conflicts among the Gaian Tribes, as well as facilitates events like the Second War of Rage.<br /> <br /> - Pentex is an investment and consulting firm that has very little on-paper involvement with the various independent companies that serve the Wyrm. They are off-the-books cultic coordinators that act as middle men between these various other corrupted businesses and the Maeljin Incarnae - but it's not one giant super-corp anywhere that can be bureaucratically tracked.<br /> <br /> - Most of Magadon's drugs are legit. It would be too easy to trace negative affects otherwise. They primarily serve the Wyrm through fomori experimentation under the auspices of medical research, and by pushing the opioid epidemic.<br /> <br /> - Children of Gaia are not a Tribe. I might feel differently if they got a decent Revised-quality Tribe Book, but they didn't, so I simply do not have a sense of them as a culture like I do the other Tribes. Instead, they exist as a multi-Tribal camp dedicated to inter-tribal peace, equality, restoring relations with the Fera, and opposing all war not directly against the Wyrm itself as feeding the Beast-of-War.<br /> <br /> - Black Tooth still lives. He and his Pride dominate southeast Africa and he names himself King of Cats. While his brutality toward all who would oppose him is horrific, he is also actually fighting the Wyrm's minions. The Ahadi exists as a resistance movement against him, but many who may hate him are reluctant to throw their support behind it because he is seen as an effective commander against the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> - Yava are largely metaphoric (I have a list of what they all actually mean), but work in many ways like &quot;True Names&quot; of the Tribe. If a Bastet knows their Tribe's Yava they are virtually immune to mind-reading and mental-influence supernatural powers from someone who does not know their Yava. If someone discovers a Tribe's Yava, members of that Tribe can not even exert the normal defensive rolls or willpower expenditures against mind-reading or supernatural mental-influences.<br /> <br /> - The Silver Crown is still missing (I'm thinking of throwing the Tribes into chaos via the &quot;Rightful King&quot; being revealed to be a Metis); Jonas Albrecht does not exist as an NPC (he's clearly someone's PC, as opposed to characters like Konetziko who comes of more as an interesting plot hook for pcs to interact with).<br /> <br /> - &quot;Lunatics&quot; do actually go through the First Change, they just completely reject their nature, and as a result cannot control their shifting, generally only doing it in Frenzy under their Auspice moon. They are in short Classic Hollywood Werewolves.<br /> <br /> - The Beast Courts are less idyllic. After all, look at the ecological disaster that is modern China - clearly not a sign they have their shit together. They are very hierarchical, and the survival of the Zhong Lung is a closely guarded secret. Generally, the Nezumi, Tengu, and any Bagheera or Garou who join have no idea, with the upper ranks of the Courts they're aware of being dominated by Khan, Same-Bito, and Kitsune, who in turn are aware of the Zhong Lung above them. Naga keep to the shadows and pass themselves off as Zhong Lung to the upper Courts when they have to.<br /> <br /> -Normal Ananasi exist in East Asia and obviously hate the Kumo.<br /> <br /> - (long list of what seem to be ParaWolf imposed edits on Changing Ways to ignore...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-30-2018, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T15:49:04-08:00","id":1180909,"title":"","content":"*double post*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-30-2018, 06:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T15:52:00-08:00","id":1180914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1180904#post1180904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd redo the Umbra in a major way.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm tinkering with the Umbra for my own table currently, so I'd be very interested to know what your thoughts are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T16:26:01-08:00","id":1180929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1180914#post1180914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm tinkering with the Umbra for my own table currently, so I'd be very interested to know what your thoughts are.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's something my group has tinkered with back when we played the games. The simplest way I can boil it down was we made it much more like the Dreaming, but obviously less of an American pop-culture sense of fairytales. There was also more of a sense of the Penumbral form of a city or forest being connected to the near-umbral general concept of cities and forests themselves. I had an idea in regards to this connection that as the gauntlet thickens it pushes the Penumbral reflection 'deeper' in the Umbra to reflect the connection to its more idealized form.<br /> <br /> What about you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 01-31-2018, 12:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T17:01:19-08:00","id":1180934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since it's WtA, it'll be finished like this:<br /> -pictures-<br /> P.S. That's what they actually deserved.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno if they deserved anything, considering that was only a representation of a mother wolf getting annoyed at her cub playing with a homid-father provided squeaky toy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T18:35:24-08:00","id":1180961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1180905#post1180905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's actually a pretty easy change. You just remove the notion that Vampires stink of this supernatural god-being they've never heard of and have nothing to do with. Conflict can still happen a lot, as with Werewolves and Mages, but it it's pretty easy to remove the Gift-ping that gives Werewolves the &quot;kill on sight&quot; default.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wyrm is not a mere deity. It is a cosmic force, and vampires are in the thrall of two out of three, since they also exhibit that desire to control others in addition to the one where they basically gather large, apathetic populations inured to violence together and use them as armor. So even if you got rid of the Wyrm's attention toward them, the Weaver would still be pulling for them... and drawing them closer. They'd have to be vampires that aren't the kind from the WoD to be the variety that aren't inherently twisted and entangled by cosmic forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T18:56:07-08:00","id":1180967,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't change much, honestly.<br /> <br /> I would, however, amp up the relationship between Pentex and the Technocracy--even more than the Syndicate/SPD connection. But I hear that's one of the possible things New White Wolf is looking at changing.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T19:17:02-08:00","id":1180973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1180967#post1180967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't change much, honestly.<br /> <br /> I would, however, amp up the relationship between Pentex and the Technocracy--even more than the Syndicate/SPD connection. But I hear that's one of the possible things New White Wolf is looking at changing.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd honestly rather any relationship be toned down, personally. To me, the Technocracy are a bunch of progressive-statist tyrants who don't care how many dead bodies or broken souls they have to pave the road toward their imagined utopia, while PENTEX is a collection of sociopathic nihilists, deranged cultists and outright freaks who want to watch the world burn and maybe get choice spot perching on the rotting carcass. Besides being monsters with nearly unfettered access to the levers of modern power, they don't really have a lot in common. But then, in my games, there are no vampires sitting on PENTEX's board, and the Syndicate are slightly different than in canon. But to each their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T19:18:41-08:00","id":1180974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1180961#post1180961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Wyrm is not a mere deity. It is a cosmic force, and vampires are in the thrall of two out of three, since they also exhibit that desire to control others in addition to the one where they basically gather large, apathetic populations inured to violence together and use them as armor. So even if you got rid of the Wyrm's attention toward them, the Weaver would still be pulling for them... and drawing them closer. They'd have to be vampires that aren't the kind from the WoD to be the variety that aren't inherently twisted and entangled by cosmic forces.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that\u2019s how you treat Sense Wyrm, yeah, but i\u2019m saying it\u2019s really easy change not to treat it that way and it makes the setting make more sense since it means Garou can actually disagree about what is and is not \u201cof the Wyrm\u201d without having an easy way to check - thus explainin how something like the Second War of Rage or the War of Tears could happen.<br /> <br /> All via the minor tweaking of one gift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T19:23:47-08:00","id":1180978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1180974#post1180974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that\u2019s how you treat Sense Wyrm, yeah, but i\u2019m saying it\u2019s really easy change not to treat it that way and it makes the setting make more sense since it means Garou can actually disagree about what is and is not \u201cof the Wyrm\u201d without having an easy way to check - thus explainin how something like the Second War of Rage or the War of Tears could happen.<br /> <br /> All via the minor tweaking of one gift.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's presently an easy way to check, but it's somewhat well known as well that various beings can mask it as well. Also, in order to really introduce ambiguity, you'd need to not call high-success frenzies &quot;Thrall of the Wyrm&quot; as an official game term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T19:25:21-08:00","id":1180979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1180973#post1180973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd honestly rather any relationship be toned down, personally. To me, the Technocracy are a bunch of progressive-statist tyrants who don't care how many dead bodies or broken souls they have to pave the road toward their imagined utopia, while PENTEX is a collection of sociopathic nihilists, deranged cultists and outright freaks who want to watch the world burn and maybe get choice spot perching on the rotting carcass. Besides being monsters with nearly unfettered access to the levers of modern power, they don't really have a lot in common. But then, in my games, there are no vampires sitting on PENTEX's board, and the Syndicate are slightly different than in canon. But to each their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing about the SPD connection is people exaggerate it into being this great alliance, or worse - i\u2019ve seen one person argue that Pentex was 1/5 of the Syndicate and thus a dwarfed component of the Technocratic Union.<br /> <br /> When what\u2019s actually the case in canon is that one conspiracy has a toe in the door via some corrupted agents in one outfit of another conspiracy. That\u2019s all it is - it\u2019s a point of corruption in the Technocracy by Pentex to facilitate the false appearance of an alliance in earlier books. Of course any Syndicate Mages actually aligned with Pentex are Malfean barabbi!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-30-2018, 10:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T20:18:08-08:00","id":1180990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1180973#post1180973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But then, in my games, there are no vampires sitting on PENTEX's board</div> </div> </div> </div>That's something I've been wrestling with as well. Zettler's existence was obviously rooted in 1st edition, when the Sabbat were generically super-evil vampires, who naturally ran in packs with Black Spiral Dancers. How the Sabbat has been defined since then makes Zettler clearly anathemic to everything the Sabbat is about. He's a Masquerade upholding executive trying to bring about what the rest of the Sabbat would see as Gehenna via what they'd see as Infernalism.<br /> <br /> On one hand part of me wants to drop a clear relic of a thinking about the Sabbat and how the gamelines interacted that stopped being canon. A Malfean Nephandi would seem a better crossover fit for the Pentex Board anyway, if one wanted a crossover.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, there's a potentially cool story about the Sabbat Inquisition closing in on Zettler!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T22:25:48-08:00","id":1181018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1180934#post1180934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno if they deserved anything, considering that was only a representation of a mother wolf getting annoyed at her cub playing with a homid-father provided squeaky toy.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they are Garou and they are breathing - any glimpse of happiness should be destroyed for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T02:42:27-08:00","id":1181057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1181018#post1181018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they are Garou and they are breathing - any glimpse of happiness should be destroyed for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regular old wolves, sadly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T08:33:36-08:00","id":1181138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1181018#post1181018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they are Garou and they are breathing - any glimpse of happiness should be destroyed for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deep breaths, bud. They aren't real, and can't hurt you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T12:09:37-08:00","id":1181183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1181138#post1181138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deep breaths, bud. They aren't real, and can't hurt you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. This thread is about what I'd change in setting. Am I allowed to dream?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> But, seriously - I would prefer something like (from crossover point of view) mysterious 'assassin brotherhood' with some unclear goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T13:02:44-08:00","id":1181202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1180990#post1180990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's something I've been wrestling with as well. Zettler's existence was obviously rooted in 1st edition, when the Sabbat were generically super-evil vampires, who naturally ran in packs with Black Spiral Dancers. How the Sabbat has been defined since then makes Zettler clearly anathemic to everything the Sabbat is about. He's a Masquerade upholding executive trying to bring about what the rest of the Sabbat would see as Gehenna via what they'd see as Infernalism.<br /> <br /> On one hand part of me wants to drop a clear relic of a thinking about the Sabbat and how the gamelines interacted that stopped being canon. A Malfean Nephandi would seem a better crossover fit for the Pentex Board anyway, if one wanted a crossover.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, there's a potentially cool story about the Sabbat Inquisition closing in on Zettler!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, a lot of the 1st ed stuff always had that &quot;I'm into X and you're into X so we should totally hang out, like, <i>all the time</i>!&quot; vibe going on. Not just the Sabbat, PENTEX and the like having World Crime League keggers at the Legion of Doom's giant Darth Vader head, but also things like the 1st ed Verbena hanging out with vampires all the time because of &quot;the power of blood&quot;, half the Garou Nation hopping up and down begging the Dreamspeakers to take them on as Acolytes, or any group that was all-female being BFFs with the Black Furies. It was something all of the revised edition developers worked to get away from. <br /> <br /> I like your idea about Zettler and the Sabbat Inquisition. That sort of thing would've made him actually interesting. <br /> <br /> (My own games have PENTEX's Board with only seven members loosely inspired by the Seven Deadly Sins, all of them mostly human, at least two - Sam Haight and one other - rogue Kinfolk, and one partially based on Damian Thorne from the Omen movies.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T13:12:20-08:00","id":1181205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1060089#post1060089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Kindred that have Humanity 7+ or Path of the Feral Heart (and presumably Road of Beast or Path of Harmony) 7+ are not considered of the Wyrm to the senses of the Fera, so they are capable of 'fitting in'. It is just the ones who are immoral, weak-willed, or faint of heart that cause the Fera problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how we play it around my table: vampires with high humanity don't have any wyrm taint, and the theory among some local garou is that they're more weaver-creatures than anything. There's even one very high-humanity vampire NPC in our WTA game who has the ability to shape-shift into a wolf and had several Garou believing she was one of them for a while. It caused big problems when they found out she's actually a leech. There also seems to be a sort of agreement between the local Bone Gnawers and vampires to &quot;live and let live&quot; as long as neither side causes the other serious problems. From the Garou perspective, tolerance of high-humanity leeches that don't smell of the wyrm may just amount to &quot;we'll kill you last,&quot; but it definitely opens a door for tolerable co-existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T13:19:06-08:00","id":1181206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1181202#post1181202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, a lot of the 1st ed stuff always had that &quot;I'm into X and you're into X so we should totally hang out, like, <i>all the time</i>!&quot; vibe going on. Not just the Sabbat, PENTEX and the like having World Crime League keggers at the Legion of Doom's giant Darth Vader head, but also things like the 1st ed Verbena hanging out with vampires all the time because of &quot;the power of blood&quot;, half the Garou Nation hopping up and down begging the Dreamspeakers to take them on as Acolytes, or any group that was all-female being BFFs with the Black Furies. It was something all of the revised edition developers worked to get away from.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Fianna had among the coldest showers in that regard, as the ties that they had to the fae proved to not be so helpful in the face of their actual adversaries and possibly some politically expedient setting up of the Ard Righ by other Garou.<br /> <br /> (That plot point could have gone way worse for the tribe without cutting off the Ard Righ, though it'd be difficult to sell a Fianna tribebook if Son of Moonlight is the leader of a vastly under-staffed tribe that had the majority of its membership vanish due to forgotten or poorly-considered oaths to the fae. It would have certainly sold the road to the Apocalypse pretty well, though.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like your idea about Zettler and the Sabbat Inquisition. That sort of thing would've made him actually interesting.<br /> <br /> (My own games have PENTEX's Board with only seven members loosely inspired by the Seven Deadly Sins, all of them mostly human, at least two - Sam Haight and one other - rogue Kinfolk, and one partially based on Damian Thorne from the Omen movies.) </div> </div> </div>Haight needs to be kept a bit less tied up than being a corporate executive if you're going to use him as an antagonist. He's a consummate middle-manager who can't be kept out of the field, so if he ends up climbing the ladder instead of trying to eat an energy field larger by far than his head, that's going to play against him. The other disgruntled Kin had better be a bit more hands off to act as a foil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T13:23:09-08:00","id":1181207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1181205#post1181205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's how we play it around my table: vampires with high humanity don't have any wyrm taint, and the theory among some local garou is that they're more weaver-creatures than anything. There's even one very high-humanity vampire NPC in our WTA game who has the ability to shape-shift into a wolf and had several Garou believing she was one of them for a while. It caused big problems when they found out she's actually a leech. There also seems to be a sort of agreement between the local Bone Gnawers and vampires to &quot;live and let live&quot; as long as neither side causes the other serious problems. From the Garou perspective, tolerance of high-humanity leeches that don't smell of the wyrm may just amount to &quot;we'll kill you last,&quot; but it definitely opens a door for tolerable co-existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do know that you're replying to a banned poster, right? There's not going to be an answer back.<br /> <br /> As to whether or not the Garou would be more comfortable with a &quot;more Weaverish&quot; standpoint on vampires, I doubt it. Even Bone Gnawers would be hard-pressed on that front, since other Weaver minions tend to try to crush their kin under jackboots and, if the Bone Gnawers in question are trying to maintain good relations with any Ratkin nearby on account of their totem being Rat, that's not going to be an incentive to tolerate vampires beyond settling the priorities of which vampires are most in need of being removed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T13:23:52-08:00","id":1181208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1058412#post1058412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on current genetic studies, I'd make the nuwisha another tribe of Garou. They betrayed the Garou during the war of rage and sided with the Fera.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really is &quot;canid soup&quot; out there in the real world.<br /> <br /> I found this on the internet a while back, and thought it was hilarious...<a href=\"https://orig00.deviantart.net/5bac/f/2012/267/5/4/you_got_your_coyotes_in_my_wolves____by_leonca-d5fryaw.png\" target=\"_blank\">https://orig00.deviantart.net/5bac/f...ca-d5fryaw.png</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://orig00.deviantart.net/5bac/f/2012/267/5/4/you_got_your_coyotes_in_my_wolves____by_leonca-d5fryaw.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T13:33:41-08:00","id":1181214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1181207#post1181207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You do know that you're replying to a banned poster, right? There's not going to be an answer back.<br /> <br /> As to whether or not the Garou would be more comfortable with a &quot;more Weaverish&quot; standpoint on vampires, I doubt it. Even Bone Gnawers would be hard-pressed on that front, since other Weaver minions tend to try to crush their kin under jackboots and, if the Bone Gnawers in question are trying to maintain good relations with any Ratkin nearby on account of their totem being Rat, that's not going to be an incentive to tolerate vampires beyond settling the priorities of which vampires are most in need of being removed.</div> </div> </div> </div>No I didn't realize that was a banned poster, but it's okay since this is a group conversation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's still definitely taboo to talk openly about leeches in those terms, and the Garou who are willing to make deals with them from time to time would fiercely deny it in public. Tolerating the high-humanity vampires may be as much a way for an urban caern to excuse the fact that they don't have the resources to win a city-wide war with the local vampires, but it's a facet of the game I'm playing in right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T14:06:36-08:00","id":1181227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1181206#post1181206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haight needs to be kept a bit less tied up than being a corporate executive if you're going to use him as an antagonist. He's a consummate middle-manager who can't be kept out of the field, so if he ends up climbing the ladder instead of trying to eat an energy field larger by far than his head, that's going to play against him. The other disgruntled Kin had better be a bit more hands off to act as a foil.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's an independent (or outside) director, effectively brought in for his unique expertise to help combat the Garou, consulting on security, First Teams and various super soldier projects and sometimes arcane matters, among other things while taking advantage of PENTEX's wide range of resources to further his own ends. The other one is an elderly society matron nursing a decades old grudge for having spent her early life as a Pure Bred brood mare for a Silver Fang house, similar in temperament to Angela Lansbury in The Manchurian Candidate (1962) and various Soap Opera Evil Matriarchs. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T16:17:07-08:00","id":1181264,"title":"","content":"I'd either change Pentex more into what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> did in his home brew or just pretend Pentex never existed. I understand it's a major part of canon, and I would never begrudge anyone who used it, but it's too silly as is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T13:08:23-08:00","id":1181476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1181264#post1181264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd either change Pentex more into what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> did in his home brew or just pretend Pentex never existed. I understand it's a major part of canon, and I would never begrudge anyone who used it, but it's too silly as is.</div> </div> </div> </div>The storyteller of the game I'm in never brings up Pentex, I think because there's plenty of pollution, corruption, abuse, etc. to draw from in the real world that he doesn't need to invoke its name. Individual tables also have the luxury of naming and using specific, real-life &quot;bad guy&quot; companies whenever they like, whereas the game publishers might have legal problems doing that. I figure Pentex is a name you can use if you want to maintain some separation of your game's world from the real world, but it's one of those things that's easy to do just fine without.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T02:02:16-08:00","id":1182836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1181202#post1181202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like your idea about Zettler and the Sabbat Inquisition. That sort of thing would've made him actually interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did like Harold the Engraver (&quot;Zettler&quot; in Middle High German), Malkavian Infernalist with his own special path Dark Thaumaturgy drawing power on the demonic bane legions of the three headed dragon he worships, making a cameo in the V20 Dark Ages Companion; which is another minor point in favor of keeping him around to use in a vampire related plotline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-06-2018, 05:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T02:31:36-08:00","id":1182840,"title":"","content":"I think the best way to do a comically evil corperation would actually be to justify the seemingly pointless/comic evil.<br /> <br /> In my games, certain banes and other evil entities will grant power for favour. Think of pouring toxic waste into the swamp as chimage for an amazing cock and a winning smile, the misery of your enemies and a blessed life. If you take a step further and lace your drugs with harmful chemicals, the spirit'll go further and grant you fame, brains, and'll ensure your profits increase for the next year. Throw a few children into a fire and you'll get a few more years to enjoy all this. You can't back out, terrible things'll happen when you do that. <br /> <br /> When you turn around and start playing vampire or mage, maybe these spirits go on offer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T22:11:59-08:00","id":1184627,"title":"","content":"A bunch of stuff<br /> <br /> Biggest one though would probably have to be the rules for determining what animals are viable breeding stock. They are already super arbitrary. <br /> <br /> Example, Bunyips breeding with Thylacine make absolutely no sense since there were more than likely dingos on the island at that time. I would make any canine close to wolves viable partners<br /> <br /> That means the Nuwisha are no longer going to be their own a separate breed. They're probably going to be a new garou tribe or the &quot;pure tribe&quot; word for ragahbash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3701-augustus-dens","name":"Augustus Dens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3701_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T23:12:34-08:00","id":1184642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Augustus Dens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1184627#post1184627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A bunch of stuff<br /> <br /> Biggest one though would probably have to be the rules for determining what animals are viable breeding stock. They are already super arbitrary.<br /> <br /> Example, Bunyips breeding with Thylacine make absolutely no sense since there were more than likely dingos on the island at that time. I would make any canine close to wolves viable partners</div> </div> </div> </div>Nitpicking purely with regard to the time table, dingoes arrived to Australia a few thousand years ago. Aboriginal Australians, however, had already been living there for tens of thousands years by the time that this happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T23:19:28-08:00","id":1184646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Augustus Dens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1184627#post1184627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Example, Bunyips breeding with Thylacine make absolutely no sense since there were more than likely dingos on the island at that time. I would make any canine close to wolves viable partners</div> </div> </div> </div>There weren't dingoes in Australia at the time. Canines didn't show up there till 4,000 years ago. Humans (and Garou with them) came 18,000 years ago. Hence the need for the Mokole ritual to adapt to their wolfless home.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not bashing your table-canon here! I've played with an alternate setting myself where coyote &amp; dingo shifters are part of the broader Werewolf tribes. I'm just providing information about the official canon if that changes anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T01:44:03-08:00","id":1184662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1184646#post1184646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There weren't dingoes in Australia at the time. Canines didn't show up there till 4,000 years ago. Humans (and Garou with them) came 18,000 years ago. Hence the need for the Mokole ritual to adapt to their wolfless home.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nitpick - humans have been living in Australia around 40-50k years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T02:03:26-08:00","id":1184666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1184646#post1184646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There weren't dingoes in Australia at the time. Canines didn't show up there till 4,000 years ago. Humans (and Garou with them) came 18,000 years ago. Hence the need for the Mokole ritual to adapt to their wolfless home.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not bashing your table-canon here! I've played with an alternate setting myself where coyote &amp; dingo shifters are part of the broader Werewolf tribes. I'm just providing information about the official canon if that changes anything.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually there's some theories that point to 12000 years ago for when the Dingos were introduced to Australia, at least that's the cut off as no remains have ever been found in Tasmania and that's when it broke off from Australia proper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T10:54:10-08:00","id":1184799,"title":"","content":"I actually only have a secondary source here, I've never read the relevant books, but I absolutely can't fathom Jonas Albrecth and his pack as being cannon. The player who talks about them obviously loves Jonas and the silver fangs are an obvious favourite. But I'm a more cynical bent and they're obviously the result of a self indulgent table thinking their chronicle should be canon. <br /> <br /> Would like to see the Shadow lords take leadership of the nation though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T11:00:11-08:00","id":1184802,"title":"","content":"A better case than the whole mess that is Australia in WtA, is the maned wolf of South America. While in a distinct from from the <i>Lupus</i> genus, they get called wolves in general language for a reason. <br /> <br /> Letting them be valid lupus kin has a bunch of positive effects: It extends the southern range of the Uktena much farther south, Letting the Wendigo and Croatoan spread out a bit more. It adds a lot of the more multicultural side of the Uktena if they have a much larger presence in the maned wolf's range, because that means a lot of presence in Brazil making it easier to draw a difference between the Uktena who are multicultural mostly due to a lack of intermarriage and combining cultures, and the Children of Gaia who are more focused on promoting diversity as a positive. It also makes the Amazon War a lot more interesting because it's not just Western Garou storming into Fera territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T11:05:01-08:00","id":1184804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PewPew</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1184799#post1184799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually only have a secondary source here, I've never read the relevant books, but I absolutely can't fathom Jonas Albrecth and his pack as being cannon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean... they are? They're all official characters and their pack is objectively in the books as something that exists. Whether you like them or not, it is what it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would like to see the Shadow lords take leadership of the nation though. </div> </div> </div><br /> Eh? What's the point though? For all that I know people don't like the BNS WtA metaplot, I'd prefer the Nation having a schism between those that stay loyal to the Fangs, and those that pick the new leadership of the Lords. The schism (esp. as a new development where individual Septs might get stuck in very precarious situations) adds a lot more story potential than a flat overthrow, and adds an &quot;epic thing for the PCs to do,&quot; in resolving the schism while the Apocalypse looms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T11:47:23-08:00","id":1184829,"title":"","content":"From the WtA artbook, proof that the rando pack is canon;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/gRGooQZ.png\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/gRGooQZ.png\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/gRGooQZ.png\" target=\"_blank\"> https://i.imgur.com/gRGooQZ.png </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div> <br /> <br /> Mind, they aren't the best written pack by far and ARE pretty weird as an example pack in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T12:02:01-08:00","id":1184833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1184662#post1184662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nitpick - humans have been living in Australia around 40-50k years.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always get that number wrong! Damn it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T12:07:58-08:00","id":1184834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1184829#post1184829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the WtA artbook, proof that the rando pack is canon;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/gRGooQZ.png\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/gRGooQZ.png\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/gRGooQZ.png\" target=\"_blank\"> https://i.imgur.com/gRGooQZ.png </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Mind, they aren't the best written pack by far and ARE pretty weird as an example pack in general.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So I've never really thought too hard on them. Aside from Evan....what are people's issue with the other two?<br /> <br /> As for the Maned Wolf, I want to say Rage Across the Amazon had them as Uktena kin....or am I bleeding in some other book into my head? (Revised Tribe? Croatan Song?) As it is though, the Uktena cover A LOT of cultural territory, especially after the death of the Croatan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 02-11-2018, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T12:10:37-08:00","id":1184835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1184804#post1184804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean... they are? They're all official characters and their pack is objectively in the books as something that exists. Whether you like them or not, it is what it is.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div> <b><i>What would YOU change in the W:tA setting?</i></b><br /><br />They're garbage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T12:18:18-08:00","id":1184837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1184834#post1184834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So I've never really thought too hard on them. Aside from Evan....what are people's issue with the other two?</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, <a href=\"https://imgur.com/oAhj2vL\" target=\"_blank\">Mari's markings</a> are kinda goofy, but that isn't a serious issue.<br /> <br /> Main issue is that they don't have a pack name nor a totem. They are pack basically because the setting says they are one. That, and its unknown if they have Anthony the Stargazer and Lupa the Silver Fang from Rage across New York as members.<br /> <br /> Poorly defined, basically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 02-11-2018, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T14:15:57-08:00","id":1184885,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23728\" data-vbnamecard=\"23728\">PewPew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;This is garbage&quot; doesn't say what you'd change. It's simply stating a dislike for something in the official setting. Dumping them from your setting is a change... though Jonas at least needs some consideration unless you're doing a much larger change since he actually matters to stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T04:43:37-08:00","id":1185105,"title":"","content":"Jonas'd work if you get rid of everything he stands for. Make him the standard silver fang, the story of his exile and silver crown is fine, but his radical deviation from silver fang norms is the kind of stuff that'd have even the more moderate fangs against him, let alone the extreme groups like raptors who'd have him dead. This needs to be cut out. His pack would be at least half-silver fang and the ones who aren't would have great loyalty to the tribe. He needs to stop flouting traditions and he needs to put his tribe before himself. <br /> <br /> His intellegence and manipulation needs a boost, or I'd rule him as a puppet for someone better. I often joke that pure breed'll hide your very obvious flaws, but among other silver fangs who've all got the same crutch it's really less relevant to letting you rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T04:54:11-08:00","id":1185108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PewPew</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1185105#post1185105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jonas'd work if you get rid of everything he stands for. Make him the standard silver fang, the story of his exile and silver crown is fine, but his radical deviation from silver fang norms is the kind of stuff that'd have even the more moderate fangs against him, let alone the extreme groups like raptors who'd have him dead. This needs to be cut out. His pack would be at least half-silver fang and the ones who aren't would have great loyalty to the tribe. He needs to stop flouting traditions and he needs to put his tribe before himself.<br /> <br /> His intellegence and manipulation needs a boost, or I'd rule him as a puppet for someone better. I often joke that pure breed'll hide your very obvious flaws, but among other silver fangs who've all got the same crutch it's really less relevant to letting you rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not so sure about other fangs being against him. I mean, more hardline folks might, but given Jonas spent years near Sept of the Green just floundering about, he was not under any raptor threat or really much of a concern to the tribe. Plus, the Fangs are far from a monolith that has the numbers to take out stragglers like him. They'd rather focus on their own sept and house politics and give much a shit about one anruth that was exiled anyway.<br /> <br /> Besides, he wasn't in the area of the most hardline of houses and his grandfather was going steadily senile, thus there would be even less of an incentive for Jonas to be killed.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T10:34:49-08:00","id":1185255,"title":"","content":"Janos is supposed to represent the resurgence of the Silverfangs rising to the challenge of the times rather that sitting on the laurels of their fathers and trying to lord it over the other tribes (BE Leaders instead of simply shouting a lot about your title and heritage, a mistake Janos himself makes a couple of times, but also realizes it) and the Silverfangs trying to be a bit different too to how they are seen and have been. The pack does have a name, it's simply &quot;Albrecht's Pack&quot; and it's totem is Falcon, they are also quite a good example of a Questing Pack with Ranked members dealing with their actions and deeds over the span of years. They operated quite solidly together in the intro comic info, a few side tales and the whole Sixth Generation thing and also during the Silver Crown and only afterwards did Evan focus more on the Native Wendigo thing, Mari went back to doing her thing in New York and helping out with the Sept of the Green and Albrecht of course was being King. <br /> <br /> I think the entire point of Albrecht's Pack is that they are supposed to look and feel more like a Player Character pack rather than an NPC pack that all comes from one Tribe (in fact Multitribal septs and packs are supposed to be more the norm as the red star glows).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T11:21:47-08:00","id":1185279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1185255#post1185255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the entire point of Albrecht's Pack is that they are supposed to look and feel more like a Player Character pack rather than an NPC pack that all comes from one Tribe (in fact Multitribal septs and packs are supposed to be more the norm as the red star glows).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. They were the very original Werewolf &quot;signature characters&quot; back when 2nd ed came out, meant to represent your typical PC pack. (Originally it was just the three of them and, IIRC, a Stargazer one, before every tribe got one with Revised.) I've heard speculation that Albrecht and Evan started as Bill and John Bridges's playtest characters back when the first edition was being written, but have never found anyone who could confirm that one way or the other. Albrecht's role in Werewolf is essentially the same as Aragorn in Lord of the Rings. the new king rising in the west and all that, bringing hope and a person to rally around in their darkest hour. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T11:56:46-08:00","id":1185293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1185255#post1185255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Janos is supposed to represent the resurgence of the Silverfangs rising to the challenge of the times rather that sitting on the laurels of their fathers and trying to lord it over the other tribes (BE Leaders instead of simply shouting a lot about your title and heritage, a mistake Janos himself makes a couple of times, but also realizes it) and the Silverfangs trying to be a bit different too to how they are seen and have been. The pack does have a name, it's simply &quot;Albrecht's Pack&quot; and it's totem is Falcon, they are also quite a good example of a Questing Pack with Ranked members dealing with their actions and deeds over the span of years. They operated quite solidly together in the intro comic info, a few side tales and the whole Sixth Generation thing and also during the Silver Crown and only afterwards did Evan focus more on the Native Wendigo thing, Mari went back to doing her thing in New York and helping out with the Sept of the Green and Albrecht of course was being King.<br /> <br /> I think the entire point of Albrecht's Pack is that they are supposed to look and feel more like a Player Character pack rather than an NPC pack that all comes from one Tribe (in fact Multitribal septs and packs are supposed to be more the norm as the red star glows).</div> </div> </div> </div>Where was the Falcon totem stated in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T14:12:13-08:00","id":1185344,"title":"","content":"Going on the fact that it's Falcon that interacts with the pack displaying several of the Totem Traits you can buy with Background Points during the comic intro and outro in the 2nd edition book. falcon also shows up in other bits of fiction relating to the pack too. Granted it could just be Falcon interceding because he's a Silverfang etc but given that they are supposed to be an example of a player pack in action then it really looks like Falcon is Totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T14:14:55-08:00","id":1185345,"title":"","content":"Though it's worth nothing that Albrecht (and a lot of Non-player &amp; ST characters in fact) does not have any BG points IN Totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T14:44:14-08:00","id":1185356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1185344#post1185344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going on the fact that it's Falcon that interacts with the pack displaying several of the Totem Traits you can buy with Background Points during the comic intro and outro in the 2nd edition book. falcon also shows up in other bits of fiction relating to the pack too. Granted it could just be Falcon interceding because he's a Silverfang etc but given that they are supposed to be an example of a player pack in action then it really looks like Falcon is Totem.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1185345#post1185345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though it's worth nothing that Albrecht (and a lot of Non-player &amp; ST characters in fact) does not have any BG points IN Totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could just be Alby being the Chosen One for fangs, at least to me. As sucky as it is, unless there is clear text that Falcon -is- their totem, it to me just falls on Alby having the Crown and being destined for greatness before he got it.<br /> <br /> There is a reason why the Silver River pack got the spotlight in the revised books, they are a more defined pack that has a name and a totem.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T14:47:32-08:00","id":1185357,"title":"","content":"I like that signature pack as what they are - examples for Player Characters. Filling that role as well as they do however, makes them less viable as NPCs specifically because they're filling roles that could be left open to player characters. That's a major reason I still have the Silver Crown missing at my table - so a PC can be the rightful king, rather than Albrecht.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T14:29:39-08:00","id":1187352,"title":"","content":"My only serious change which is something I personally changed in my own game revolves around side stepping through the gauntlet. <br /> <br /> I like to insist on a reflective surface to even attempt the feat and I don\u2019t just mean polishing your glaive or a hand mirror but something that\u2019s at least big enough for the garou to pass through. In modern times it means it\u2019s very hard to find something like that in the wild beyond a river, stream or pond. Although if the guanlet is weak enough it\u2019s possible to do this without aid or by accident. Looking sideways is done in a similar way meaning it is possible to look before you jump as it were. <br /> <br /> I imagine the process as the garou walking or crawling through a mirror and walking out of the same mirror in the version of the umbra for the current location.<br /> <br /> This major change does change the dynamic to how the game is played. Yes the umbra becomes a more distant realm but it would (in my opinion) stop being a crutch for the group to lean on. It\u2019s more interesting to me when the various are not constantly looking sideways and jumps sideways to do a drive by clawing of spirits before running off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":982,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/982-cptmachine","user":"Cptmachine","date":". 02-18-2018, 05:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/982-cptmachine","name":"Cptmachine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar982_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T15:51:05-08:00","id":1187370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cptmachine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1187352#post1187352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only serious change which is something I personally changed in my own game revolves around side stepping through the gauntlet.<br /> <br /> I like to insist on a reflective surface to even attempt the feat and I don\u2019t just mean polishing your glaive or a hand mirror but something that\u2019s at least big enough for the garou to pass through. In modern times it means it\u2019s very hard to find something like that in the wild beyond a river, stream or pond. Although if the guanlet is weak enough it\u2019s possible to do this without aid or by accident. Looking sideways is done in a similar way meaning it is possible to look before you jump as it were.<br /> <br /> I imagine the process as the garou walking or crawling through a mirror and walking out of the same mirror in the version of the umbra for the current location.<br /> <br /> This major change does change the dynamic to how the game is played. Yes the umbra becomes a more distant realm but it would (in my opinion) stop being a crutch for the group to lean on. It\u2019s more interesting to me when the various are not constantly looking sideways and jumps sideways to do a drive by clawing of spirits before running off.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's interesting! I might try that. I'm inclined to make an exception for stepping sideways in Caerns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T23:11:31-08:00","id":1187469,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">1) More Protectorates, fewer actual Caerns. Not everyplace has to be magical to be considered 'home' and worth protecting.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b2) Less War of Rage, more.. big predators living too close together and competing for resources. The missing Breeds didn't die out over the course of a few years, but over the course of centuries.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b3) More focus on Kinfolk doing Kinfolk things, less Garou (or other breeds) in boardrooms. (This includes Path Dancer Uktena being mostly about protecting human/kin shamans than learning it themselves).<br /> <br /> 4</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">) The Garou Nation being less monolithic, and more locally inclined. </span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b5) Less 'Noble Savage' myth. War and Misery were not Eurpean inventions.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b6) Kill the Bubasti and Ceilican completely, move them over to being small wildcats of Eurasia and Africa and spreading quickly. This is precipitated by a (PC led) ritual killing of the last of the ghouled Kyphur the Settites keep. The Ritual cleanses the growing taint, freeing the Bubasti of the flaw of becoming tainted as they learn human magic (which as per 3, would be mostly Kin). True to the prophecy.. the Bubasti are no longer in Egypt. The new Tribe comes rushing in to give the Settites headaches. Plot hooks for Wheel of Ptah.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b7) Yava become less actual weaknesses, and more of a 'true name' fragment</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b8) Handle Ligon (and other mixed breed Bastet) metis<br /> <br /> \u200b9) Watch for spots where flavor text isn't being supported by mechanics. (IE Simba ties to the Sun vs Kahn ties, Simba heavy on flavor, but Kahn have the Yava and lower level on Fire Roar... when Roaring and Fire are a Simba thing.)</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T07:53:42-08:00","id":1187551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1187469#post1187469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b2) Less War of Rage, more.. big predators living too close together and competing for resources. The missing Breeds didn't die out over the course of a few years, but over the course of centuries.<br /> <br /> \u200b3) More focus on Kinfolk doing Kinfolk things, less Garou (or other breeds) in boardrooms. (This includes Path Dancer Uktena being mostly about protecting human/kin shamans than learning it themselves).<br /> <br /> 4) The Garou Nation being less monolithic, and more locally inclined.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like those, and actually think I handle most of these in the way described.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T16:31:05-08:00","id":1187681,"title":"","content":"One thing I'd like to change a lot, is the depiction of wolves as inherently more spiritual than humans. They might see and know there to be more supernatural things than humans, that being a common trope with canines and felines in stories, but stuff like wolves instinctively knowing how to worship (thank you, Changing Ways) and thank Gaia for their prey is a little silly.<br /> <br /> To me, the noble wolf trope takes away from the fact that the ability to truly go into metaphysics of faith is the strenght and weakness both of humanity. Giving garou, even Red Talons, their ability to respect Gaia beyond what an animal would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T14:36:21-08:00","id":1188303,"title":"","content":"Something I would change:<br /> <br /> \u200bThe downfall of the Special Affairs Department. I'd push that up to 2017 and make it an indirect result of the Trump election. Basically Gerald Osbourne was written as being in tight with the old-school Republicans. Have Martin Fiske (the crazy white-nationalist -- and possible Black Spiral Kinfolk) have some sort of nebulous connection to Steve Bannon (who practically screams Wyrm-Taint all by himself), and when Director Comey gets sacked, Osbourne quietly gets swept away as well and with some shadowy machinations, Fiske becomes the new SAD director. Then in a semi-comedic parody of the ongoing sh**-show in the rest of Washington, Fiske promptly implodes under his own personal flavor of crazy/stupid and winds up taking down the rest of the SAD with him.<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: Oh, and all the vampires are afterwards looking at each other and going: &quot;Did <i>you</i> do that? Who was behind that?&quot;, and be convinced that it <i>had</i> to be a Kindred plot of some sort... but it's actually just good old human stupidity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 02-21-2018, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T11:53:21-08:00","id":1188591,"title":"","content":"I have considered two changes with regard to lineage and breeding. First, I think the breed of a Garou (or kinfolk offspring) should be determined by the non-Garou parent, not the mother. It's just weird to me (even considering the premise and all that) that an ordinary human man could have ordinary wolves as his biological children, if his mate were a lupus Garou.<br /> <br /> The other thing would be making all shifter kinfolk non breed specific. That is, a human is simply kinfolk or not, rather than Garou kin, or Gurahl kin, or whatever specifically. Children of two kinfolk who undergo the change would favor their most recent shifter ancestor 99% of the time, making throwbacks rare. Family is still family in the conventional sense, of course, but it would add control of kinfolk populations as a point of conflict between breeds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13544-impeesa","name":"Impeesa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T01:22:10-08:00","id":1189151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Impeesa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1188591#post1188591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have considered two changes with regard to lineage and breeding. First, I think the breed of a Garou (or kinfolk offspring) should be determined by the non-Garou parent, not the mother. It's just weird to me (even considering the premise and all that) that an ordinary human man could have ordinary wolves as his biological children, if his mate were a lupus Garou.<br /> <br /> The other thing would be making all shifter kinfolk non breed specific. That is, a human is simply kinfolk or not, rather than Garou kin, or Gurahl kin, or whatever specifically. Children of two kinfolk who undergo the change would favor their most recent shifter ancestor 99% of the time, making throwbacks rare. Family is still family in the conventional sense, of course, but it would add control of kinfolk populations as a point of conflict between breeds.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first part is a fairly common alteration, with the mother being forced to remain in the child's form instead of breed form for the later part of the pregnancy, and is one I considered adding. However, I've had a lot of fun with 'odd' Kin from the current setup, and don't mind it. (I also toyed with it requiring the CoG Rite, one more commonly known amongst other Breeds, for cross breeding in that manner.<br /> <br /> The other possibility is changing Garou to being 'fully human' in human form and 'fully wolf' in wolf form. (IE, for purposes of Silver and Regeneration) rather than being 'out of breed form' being something vastly superior to natural examples of it.<br /> <br /> For the second, that would require a significant shift in Kinfolk. Keeping in mind Pure Breed still being the carrying of a family lineage, and access to Gifts that still acknowledge type. Additionally, Kinfolk aren't about 'weak breeding stock', they are <i>family. </i>Being just generic breeding stock turns them into cattle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T00:37:45-08:00","id":1191280,"title":"","content":"Wow, I am going to have to sit down and read the whole Topic! But what I wanted to change is about spirits in World of darkness (mostly werewolf). they are one of the few things that are plot devices but over time, they have expanded to all games.<br /> <br /> I wanted to first make them look like other Player Characters! then centralize concepts in a spiritual point of view!<br /> <br /> Like:<br /> making sure the spirit can teach the gifts it is on the hook for<br /> making sure the powers that a possessed being has lined up to spirit charms<br /> making states that are unique to them yet fit in the world 's makeup!<br /> Make them a character sheet<br /> <br /> the list goes on!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>&quot;Don't worry, it'll work out somehow.&quot; - <br /> <i>You Asakura (Shaman King)</i></b><br /><br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23653-alstonjc","name":"Alstonjc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T03:01:12-07:00","id":1194188,"title":"","content":"Really, there are only two main things I would change about WtA. One is a bit subtle and the other subjective.<br /> <br /> Firstly, WtA is an oddball of all the WoD setting, in that it largely forgets/ignors teal world religions in favor of it's definitive Gaian cosmology. In all of the other games, the truth of reality is unknown. Maybe Caine existed, maybe not. But just because Caine did, that does not mean G_d/The One Above also did. In Mage, who the hell knows. I mean, literally, a monkey might have Awakened and rewritten the very fabric of everything to be the world we now know, or Pagan faiths are real, or there is no divinity, or whatever. All are viable, though perhaps not equally viable.<br /> <br /> WtA, however, essentially establishes that Gaia, the Triad, spirits, etc... are all 100% factual things. But that leaves a lot of real world faiths, well badically unrepresented in a setting that is suppossed to be set in a real-world-like place somewhere between the X Files and Sin City, making say a fervent Muslim Garou, well stupid. I know, thinking too hard about it and it makes no sense, but it has been in the setting since the start.<br /> <br /> Now, I am NOT saying drop Gaia, the Triad, and all the Garou mythology. Instead, I simply mean to make it more of a faith than a fact. Present it as one of the most commonly held rationalizations by trying to incorporate various Tribe's stories, (with a shit load of inconsitencies), but with some things unexplainable.<br /> <br /> Secondly, focus a bit more on Garou being monstrous rather than <i>as</i> heroic. Like I mentioned, a bit subjective, and Revised tried this a bit. So it is kind of hard to say just how much this would need to change, table to table. We see some, off screen, about how bad Garou are to kinfolk, and there is the occasional &quot;oh, my bad&quot; for Rage/Frenzy, but these seem mostly swept under the rug because no one really knows the real truth of the universe as a Gaian warrior.<br /> <br /> Anyway, those are my two thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T03:51:42-07:00","id":1194200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194188#post1194188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, there are only two main things I would change about WtA. One is a bit subtle and the other subjective.<br /> <br /> Firstly, WtA is an oddball of all the WoD setting, in that it largely forgets/ignors teal world religions in favor of it's definitive Gaian cosmology. In all of the other games, the truth of reality is unknown. Maybe Caine existed, maybe not. But just because Caine did, that does not mean G_d/The One Above also did. In Mage, who the hell knows. I mean, literally, a monkey might have Awakened and rewritten the very fabric of everything to be the world we now know, or Pagan faiths are real, or there is no divinity, or whatever. All are viable, though perhaps not equally viable.<br /> <br /> WtA, however, essentially establishes that Gaia, the Triad, spirits, etc... are all 100% factual things. But that leaves a lot of real world faiths, well badically unrepresented in a setting that is suppossed to be set in a real-world-like place somewhere between the X Files and Sin City, making say a fervent Muslim Garou, well stupid. I know, thinking too hard about it and it makes no sense, but it has been in the setting since the start.<br /> <br /> Now, I am NOT saying drop Gaia, the Triad, and all the Garou mythology. Instead, I simply mean to make it more of a faith than a fact. Present it as one of the most commonly held rationalizations by trying to incorporate various Tribe's stories, (with a shit load of inconsitencies), but with some things unexplainable.<br /> <br /> Secondly, focus a bit more on Garou being monstrous rather than <i>as</i> heroic. Like I mentioned, a bit subjective, and Revised tried this a bit. So it is kind of hard to say just how much this would need to change, table to table. We see some, off screen, about how bad Garou are to kinfolk, and there is the occasional &amp;quot;oh, my bad&amp;quot; for Rage/Frenzy, but these seem mostly swept under the rug because no one really knows the real truth of the universe as a Gaian warrior.<br /> <br /> Anyway, those are my two thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those two thoughts won\u2019t be exclusive to you, since the <i>lack</i> of such elements is one of the reasons that kept me away from this game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T03:53:18-07:00","id":1194201,"title":"","content":"I know its not unique to me, but I also know that a very vocal WtA fanbase here is very against it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T08:56:04-07:00","id":1194264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194201#post1194201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know its not unique to me, but I also know that a very vocal WtA fanbase here is very against it.</div> </div> </div> </div>As one of the aformentioned fanbase, for me the garou as monsters theme would undercut the fact that garou are people. People can be very very good or very very bad, and that to me is the crux of the issues in WtA. It is people from various sides and various viewpoints clashing against one another while trying to save the world. In a culture that endorses child abuse, domestic slavery, ableism and just plain old murder. Yet, these are very much our only hope and some do rise above the stereotypes of their culture.<br /> <br /> To paint garou as monsters, it takes away the fact that they always could have chosen to -not- do the horrid things that they did. That they could have as easily used their influence for the better. But they didn't, instead becoming an abusive horror to their kinfolk and those weaker than them. A monster is what monster does, it never had a choice for the contrary. That isn't very interesting to me, as there was never a chance it could have chosen another path.<br /> <br /> Then again, I see pretty much any WoD character as a person. No matter how horrid the deed, a human has done it and done -worse-.<br /> <br /> In terms of the world building, if garou were to be more darker than they are, then BSDs and the Wyrm should not be such a legit threat to the world and not as clearly in the wrong. Otherwise, there is too much dark. BSDs are not player characters, because they are out to just defile and destroy and rape and all that. Sabbat still has a goal that is in theory noble, and they don't have underground breeding pits with radiation. Even if a BSD is relatively reasonable, they do still partake in those above activities without a question.<br /> <br /> I think Werewolf the Forsaken tried to even the scales and make the Uratha more vague. By second edition, they succeeded. Only issue is that the Pure are still pretty mustache twirly and so don't really make you go 'but what if they are in the right?'. The situation being ambigious is when I myself am more open to having no side clearly be better than the other.<br /> <br /> Please note that it isn't because I'm squeamish about darker things. While my favourite clan is Tzimisce, I am often tired of the cenobite aping Tzimi whose whole shtick is that. Not because I find it gruesome, but because it says nothing of the character themselves. Then again, I do not consider Cenobites themselves to be evil. They are creatures of excess sensations, coming when called fort. They are neither good or evil, they just are. The tzimisce who takes that role isn't a spirit, they once were a human. There has to be more to them than seeking sensations or gore, because they never truly stopped being a person even after embrace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 03-11-2018, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T10:46:40-07:00","id":1194298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194264#post1194264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then again, I do not consider Cenobites themselves to be evil. They are creatures of excess sensations, coming when called fort. They are neither good or evil, they just are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to derail...but that's what Clive Barker was going for with his novel, it was everyone else involved in the Hell Raiser film franchise that messed that up.<br /> <br /> (Just wanted to affirm that you're right)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T11:10:06-07:00","id":1194304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194298#post1194298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not to derail...but that's what Clive Barker was going for with his novel, it was everyone else involved in the Hell Raiser film franchise that messed that up.<br /> <br /> (Just wanted to affirm that you're right)</div> </div> </div> </div>It goes into my point, tbh. Making the cenobites into evil monsters seeking world domination took away what made them so interesting. The cenobites don't just randomly attack people, they need to be summoned by people who are in the know of a puzzle box, and who have enough will and ennui to solve it. In the second movie (which I think was written by Barker?) they even let the girl who solved the puzzle for a doctor be as SHE was not the real person wanting them around. The evil, therefore, comes from the humans that seek them.<br /> <br /> Such moral grayness works if it isn't contrasted by something darker. Garou are the heroes as long as Wyrm and its minions are around. This is why any morally very gray WtA games should either take place in the middle ages or before, or post-apocalypse where it becomes garou vs garou.<br /> <br /> Plus, the issues with kinfolk abuse and destructive frenzies are stuff that the ST running the game has to enforce. The books can't help if the game itself isn't pushing that angle.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T11:30:52-07:00","id":1194306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194304#post1194304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It goes into my point, tbh. Making the cenobites into evil monsters seeking world domination took away what made them so interesting. The cenobites don't just randomly attack people, they need to be summoned by people who are in the know of a puzzle box, and who have enough will and ennui to solve it. In the second movie (which I think was written by Barker?) they even let the girl who solved the puzzle for a doctor be as SHE was not the real person wanting them around. The evil, therefore, comes from the humans that seek them.<br /> <br /> Such moral grayness works if it isn't contrasted by something darker. Garou are the heroes as long as Wyrm and its minions are around. This is why any morally very gray WtA games should either take place in the middle ages or before, or post-apocalypse where it becomes garou vs garou.<br /> <br /> Plus, the issues with kinfolk abuse and destructive frenzies are stuff that the ST running the game has to enforce. The books can't help if the game itself isn't pushing that angle.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Right again on Hellraiser II being written by Barker. The movies went down hill after they lost site of what makes cenobites unique in horror. <br /> <br /> Anyway, its why I like WtA so much. You CAN have your grey, its just against something like the forces of the forces of the Wyrm its easy to mistake the middle ground as either black or white. I have an antagonist in my game that's a Nuwisha, who frequently messes with the players. They are convinced he's evil and of the wyrm because he puts them in dangerous situations, and at times creates problems for them with other Gaian forces. The fun is, my players are convinced he is evil IC and OOC because people mistake &quot;not with us&quot; as evil, and &quot;with us&quot; as good so easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 03-11-2018, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T11:59:09-07:00","id":1194314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cptmachine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1187352#post1187352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only serious change which is something I personally changed in my own game revolves around side stepping through the gauntlet.<br /> <br /> I like to insist on a reflective surface to even attempt the feat and I don\u2019t just mean polishing your glaive or a hand mirror but something that\u2019s at least big enough for the garou to pass through. In modern times it means it\u2019s very hard to find something like that in the wild beyond a river, stream or pond. Although if the guanlet is weak enough it\u2019s possible to do this without aid or by accident. Looking sideways is done in a similar way meaning it is possible to look before you jump as it were.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do the exact same thing. It annoys players, but they get used to it. I don't want stepping sideways to be mundane or something can happen anytime it is convenient. Players have to plan for it. It makes jaunts into the umbra more like an actual spirit quest. Of course that goes the same for the bad guys as well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T12:31:22-07:00","id":1194326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194188#post1194188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, there are only two main things I would change about WtA. One is a bit subtle and the other subjective.<br /> <br /> Firstly, WtA is an oddball of all the WoD setting, in that it largely forgets/ignors teal world religions in favor of it's definitive Gaian cosmology. In all of the other games, the truth of reality is unknown. Maybe Caine existed, maybe not. But just because Caine did, that does not mean G_d/The One Above also did. In Mage, who the hell knows. I mean, literally, a monkey might have Awakened and rewritten the very fabric of everything to be the world we now know, or Pagan faiths are real, or there is no divinity, or whatever. All are viable, though perhaps not equally viable.<br /> <br /> WtA, however, essentially establishes that Gaia, the Triad, spirits, etc... are all 100% factual things. But that leaves a lot of real world faiths, well badically unrepresented in a setting that is suppossed to be set in a real-world-like place somewhere between the X Files and Sin City, making say a fervent Muslim Garou, well stupid. I know, thinking too hard about it and it makes no sense, but it has been in the setting since the start.<br /> <br /> Now, I am NOT saying drop Gaia, the Triad, and all the Garou mythology. Instead, I simply mean to make it more of a faith than a fact. Present it as one of the most commonly held rationalizations by trying to incorporate various Tribe's stories, (with a shit load of inconsitencies), but with some things unexplainable.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my games I try to run it that the Garou have sufficient knowledge that there are things they know to a great detail (the Middle Umbra), but they are actually quite ignorant about a lot of things (everything else). And their mythology, while correct in many broad strokes, simplifies lots of things and ignores other. This means more work for me as an ST, as I have to know the &quot;real&quot; truth which is different from how the Garou NPCs understand it. The PCs know what the Garou think (what's in the core book), and it is up to them to figure out if anything is different (and does it matter from a practical perspective).<br /> <br /> The Triat is real in the sense that Mage tells us that Dynamism, Stasis, and Entropy are real. But the Triat is simply anthroposized versions of the Metaphysic Trinity. Much like the old koan that if You see the Buddha, Kill the Buddha, if the Garou ever encounter the Wyld, Weaver, or Wyrm, it must assuredly is not. That does not mean the Garou have reached their level of understanding - they obviously have not. Certain individual Garou (most likely Theurges, especially from tribes like Stargazers, Children of Gaia, and Uktena) might have realized this. They might even have brought up the subject now and then, but the reaction from all other Garou convince them that is not a wise thing to do (you don't cast pearls before swine, especially if they might kill you because of it) so they keep silent.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Wyrm&quot; is simply their explanation for the Problem of Evil in philosophy, and anytime they discover something they don't like, they call it that even if they're not really related. Demons from the High Umbra are the Wyrm as are Spectres from the Dark Umbra, as are any minions in the Middle Umbra they corrupt. As are Deep Umbral invaders whose presence here is toxic to the biosphere (the Martian's Red Weed from HG Wells, the Thing in Carpenter's 1982 movie, Lovecraft's Colours Out of Space). Primal forces of Chaos like Titans, Jotuns, and Dragons that would unmake everything back to where it was (which are the original opponents of the Garou). Mages make distinctions between the various Nephandi, but the Garou would see that as mere sophistry. Perhaps useful in some way, but it dangerously goes down a path of relativism that might undermine their fanaticism which is needed to destroy the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> But my perspective is based from my initial exposure to the game lines in First Edition when everything was one huge game, and I use a more Lovecraftian or Cosmic Horror interpretation in my Werewolf games which means the Garou actually don't know everything and can often be wrong. In practice, being wrong does not necessarily mean the Garou can't end the immediate threat. They are really good at that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Secondly, focus a bit more on Garou being monstrous rather than <i>as</i> heroic. Like I mentioned, a bit subjective, and Revised tried this a bit. So it is kind of hard to say just how much this would need to change, table to table. We see some, off screen, about how bad Garou are to kinfolk, and there is the occasional &quot;oh, my bad&quot; for Rage/Frenzy, but these seem mostly swept under the rug because no one really knows the real truth of the universe as a Gaian warrior. </div> </div> </div>I actually think Revised went in the other direction, eliminating the obviously monstrous in favor of some kind of epic high fantasy. For instance, almost every tribe had an obviously monstrous camp in the original tribebooks. Multiple tribes had camps which encouraged eating people. There were lots of camps that existed merely to go after and fight other tribes. There were camps that dealt with a lot of forbidden knowledge with the arrogance that they would learn more about the Wyrm, but not be corrupted by it. Lots of things that an ST could use to bring division, conflict, and establish enemies within the Garou. And most of that was wiped out in Revised.<br /> <br /> From their own perspective, the Garou should be heroic - Bronze Age Greek Myths of heroes. From humanity's perspective however, they should see them as dangerous monsters - folklore and many movies. From the kinfolk's perspective, they should see Garou as tragic creatures killing other monsters - the perspective of Lon Chaney, Jr movies. This takes work from the ST to keep this up, but it can work well. Just don't fall into the temptation to gloss over over or avoid those aspects of the Garou which conflict with their own prejudices (we're heroes) but confirms those of humans and kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T12:36:49-07:00","id":1194328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Impeesa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1188591#post1188591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have considered two changes with regard to lineage and breeding. First, I think the breed of a Garou (or kinfolk offspring) should be determined by the non-Garou parent, not the mother. It's just weird to me (even considering the premise and all that) that an ordinary human man could have ordinary wolves as his biological children, if his mate were a lupus Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do the same. I understand the reasons for that decision, but the non-Garou mate being the deciding breed just makes too much sense to me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T13:07:37-07:00","id":1194338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194188#post1194188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, there are only two main things I would change about WtA. One is a bit subtle and the other subjective.<br /> <br /> Firstly, WtA is an oddball of all the WoD setting, in that it largely forgets/ignors teal world religions in favor of it's definitive Gaian cosmology. In all of the other games, the truth of reality is unknown. Maybe Caine existed, maybe not. But just because Caine did, that does not mean G_d/The One Above also did. In Mage, who the hell knows. I mean, literally, a monkey might have Awakened and rewritten the very fabric of everything to be the world we now know, or Pagan faiths are real, or there is no divinity, or whatever. All are viable, though perhaps not equally viable.<br /> <br /> WtA, however, essentially establishes that Gaia, the Triad, spirits, etc... are all 100% factual things. But that leaves a lot of real world faiths, well badically unrepresented in a setting that is suppossed to be set in a real-world-like place somewhere between the X Files and Sin City, making say a fervent Muslim Garou, well stupid. I know, thinking too hard about it and it makes no sense, but it has been in the setting since the start.<br /> <br /> Now, I am NOT saying drop Gaia, the Triad, and all the Garou mythology. Instead, I simply mean to make it more of a faith than a fact. Present it as one of the most commonly held rationalizations by trying to incorporate various Tribe's stories, (with a shit load of inconsitencies), but with some things unexplainable.<br /> <br /> Secondly, focus a bit more on Garou being monstrous rather than <i>as</i> heroic. Like I mentioned, a bit subjective, and Revised tried this a bit. So it is kind of hard to say just how much this would need to change, table to table. We see some, off screen, about how bad Garou are to kinfolk, and there is the occasional &quot;oh, my bad&quot; for Rage/Frenzy, but these seem mostly swept under the rug because no one really knows the real truth of the universe as a Gaian warrior.<br /> <br /> Anyway, those are my two thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a crossover-friendly person, this is my go-to.<br /> <br /> Garou interact with Umbral Spirits, and the ones who are in the Garou Nation generally hold up the Triat and Gaia as facts. However, it's just one way of looking at things.<br /> <br /> It's entirely possible that the Garou's understanding of the world might be completely wrong. Then again, they might be right, or half-right. Same as with literally everyone else. So a faithful Muslim or Buddhist or Christian or an ardent Atheist who go through the First Change won't necessarily find themselves revising all that they believe (well, at the same time they might). A Christian might decide that everything they're experiencing is just a different side to life that they weren't aware of, but that doesn't mean that the Christian message is wrong. The Old Testament and New Testament are heavy on spirits that lie outside of God's direct purview, for example. An Atheist might argue that this is all rational and scientific, simply a rational and scientific part of reality that she doesn't understand. The existence of a spiritual plane doesn't automatically signify that there must be some divine creator who is worthy of worship.<br /> <br /> Another change I make is that Spirits are less... like multi-tools. Spirits are teachers and guides, they give Garou and understanding of the world, they teach Gifts, and they can be your allies. What they most certainly are not is CCTV, attack dogs or henchmen.<br /> <br /> &quot;I ask the Spirit if they saw someone running past.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The Stag Spirit does not seem to understand the question; it occurs to you that whether or not someone has just run past doesn't full under the auspice of the animistic representation of local deer.&quot;<br /> <br /> The idea is that spirits are properly alien, and they are concerned with things that are very different from what concerns humans (and Werewolves). A Tree Spirit can't tell you if someone just ran past and what way they went, but it can express its sorrow at the constant pollution of the soil, and help you get a sense of what is causing the pollution. Likewise the Stag would be able to help you if you were searching for a game hunter who was killing wolves and deer in the area. And as always, these Spirits can help with teaching Gifts, Abilities and Attributes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-11-2018, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T13:15:01-07:00","id":1194340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1180990#post1180990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's something I've been wrestling with as well. Zettler's existence was obviously rooted in 1st edition, when the Sabbat were generically super-evil vampires, who naturally ran in packs with Black Spiral Dancers. How the Sabbat has been defined since then makes Zettler clearly anathemic to everything the Sabbat is about. He's a Masquerade upholding executive trying to bring about what the rest of the Sabbat would see as Gehenna via what they'd see as Infernalism.<br /> <br /> On one hand part of me wants to drop a clear relic of a thinking about the Sabbat and how the gamelines interacted that stopped being canon. A Malfean Nephandi would seem a better crossover fit for the Pentex Board anyway, if one wanted a crossover.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, there's a potentially cool story about the Sabbat Inquisition closing in on Zettler!</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat is a &quot;House of Contradictions&quot;, first and foremost.<br /> <br /> Down with Elder Worship!<br /> <br /> Pay no attention to the Elders behind the curtain!<br /> <br /> You have what amounts to Elder worship among the Lasombra and the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> Down with Infernalism!<br /> <br /> Pay no attention to the Infernals behind the curtain!<br /> <br /> Koldunism is dangerously close to being infernal, and is only tolerated (canonically) for political reasons. You cannot call such powerful Cainites infernalists, or call the Inquisition on them. Same goes with the Abyss Mystics, who are really antithetical to the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Freedom! Freedom from control and tyranny!<br /> <br /> Please try and ignore the Bishops dosing up the Vaulderie at huge events with greater and greater doses of their blood!<br /> <br /> Zettler is working with a group that is really antithetical to the Sabbat. What else is new? If he's bringing in allies and resources for whatever Cainite is &quot;above&quot; him in the Sabbat, then he's doing fine. Until he isn't. House of contradictions and all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T15:52:17-07:00","id":1194382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194188#post1194188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> WtA, however, essentially establishes that Gaia, the Triad, spirits, etc... are all 100% factual things. But that leaves a lot of real world faiths, well badically unrepresented in a setting that is suppossed to be set in a real-world-like place...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bBasically, everybody else beat me to it, but what the heck. The biggest difference is that for the most part every other supernatural in the World of Darkness isn't really sure what the actual truth is. The Garou, on the other paw are <i>certain</i> that they're right -- because they're religious zealots. To quote Josh Billings (who is often misquoted as Samuel Clemens) &quot;\u200bIt ain't what you don't know that gets you into trouble. It's what you know for sure that just ain't so.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd that also nicely explains the monster / hero paradox of the Garou. If they're right, then they're pretty much heroes -- if they're not, then they're basically Al Qaeda with superpowers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T17:10:41-07:00","id":1194397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194382#post1194382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">basically Al Qaeda with superpowers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm agreeing up until this point.<br /> <br /> For all of the faults of the Garou Nation, I feel like they are deeply flawed in a way which is a few steps above most radical religious organisations. Even if everything they believe is wrong, a fomor who eats babies is a fomor who eats babies. They aren't necessarily getting rid of it for &quot;humanitarian&quot; reasons, but the overall result is good for humanity, in the simple day-to-day &quot;how many monsters are there?&quot; issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T00:25:42-07:00","id":1194455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194397#post1194397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm agreeing up until this point.<br /> <br /> For all of the faults of the Garou Nation, I feel like they are deeply flawed in a way which is a few steps above most radical religious organisations. Even if everything they believe is wrong, a fomor who eats babies is a fomor who eats babies. They aren't necessarily getting rid of it for &amp;quot;humanitarian&amp;quot; reasons, but the overall result is good for humanity, in the simple day-to-day &amp;quot;how many monsters are there?&amp;quot; issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do love me some Grey vs. Black conflicts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T02:50:07-07:00","id":1194473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194397#post1194397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Even if everything they believe is wrong, a fomor who eats babies is a fomor who eats babies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I stand by my position. <br /> <br /> 1. Red Talons eat babies.<br /> <br /> \u200b2. Even Ayman Al Zawahiri (leader of Al Qaeda) thought that Islamic State had gone too far down the evil ladder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T03:08:38-07:00","id":1194477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194473#post1194473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I stand by my position.<br /> <br /> 1. Red Talons eat babies.<br /> <br /> \u200b2. Even Ayman Al Zawahiri (leader of Al Qaeda) thought that Islamic State had gone too far down the evil ladder.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Red Talons do not eat babies. Even the Red Talons that consider extermination of humanity as a good are treated as fringe/crazy by the garou nation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T03:37:23-07:00","id":1194480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194473#post1194473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I stand by my position.<br /> <br /> 1. Red Talons eat babies.<br /> <br /> \u200b2. Even Ayman Al Zawahiri (leader of Al Qaeda) thought that Islamic State had gone too far down the evil ladder.</div> </div> </div> </div>I respect your position, but painting the whole Nation by the Red Talon brush is still very misleading. Not to mention, as much as the Nation jokes about Red Talons doing that, the Talons have rites and gifts meant to -hide- the human eating from the rest of the Nation. As in, if they were caught, they would be heavily punished. Going by their tribebook, their position of 'we were not there when this no-eat-human law was set' is pretty much portrayed as them trying to justify going against the Litany.<br /> <br /> But to the above point on terrorism, the Red Talon tribebook actually makes a direct comparison to them and terrorism of today ( the book was published in the early 00s), on page 100 of the revised. So, yeah, they are pretty much terrorists who think they are justified.<br /> <br /> But the Talons are a really fringe tribe that is not expecting to survive at all. Distanced by the rest of the Nation by the lack of human kinfolk. Other tribes HAVE humans they care about and so any tries to actually eradicate them would be very hard to justify to themselves.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T03:54:03-07:00","id":1194481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194382#post1194382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bBasically, everybody else beat me to it, but what the heck. The biggest difference is that for the most part every other supernatural in the World of Darkness isn't really sure what the actual truth is. The Garou, on the other paw are <i>certain</i> that they're right -- because they're religious zealots.</div> </div> </div> </div> That is the thing. It is not because they are religious zealots, (they are), but rather because they can literally interact with these beings, converse with ancestors, and otherwise know factually that that, (their whole belief system), is how it works.<br /> <br /> As written, one really can not, (rationally/realistically) interpret the spirits as say angels, devas, or most non-shamanistic real world entities. One can, but they are basically crazy, and while some of the spirits are real world religion gods, that is pretty problematic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T05:17:19-07:00","id":1194494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194264#post1194264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As one of the aformentioned fanbase, for me the garou as monsters theme would undercut the fact that garou are people.</div> </div> </div> </div>While this is true, and I agree, (really for everyone, Vampires, Magi, whatever), this is not really the tyoe of monstrosity I mean. Vampires, for instance MUST feed. They can otherwise be &quot;good&quot;, feeding from animals or butcher shops, or whatever, but those are temporary. Secondarily, over time they loose more of their &quot;goodness&quot;, and many of their needs and desires are unethical to humanity. Changlings sort of psuedo-abduct (infect?) humanity and try to manipulate them to believe a certain way so they can feed from them as well. Mages try to push their personal agendas and entire systems of beliefs on the world, possibly changing reality in ways that suit them individually. Things like that. <br /> <br /> Garou don't really have anything like that. Them being asshats and bullies is more mass individual choice than nature of their race, similar to how some vampires are bad to Ghouls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T06:21:02-07:00","id":1194504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194494#post1194494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Garou don't really have anything like that. Them being asshats and bullies is more mass individual choice than nature of their race, similar to how some vampires are bad to Ghouls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Garou do, but like the kinfolk issue, it is so reliant on the ST running it that it can be easy to just miss or not have it at all in the game.<br /> <br /> Garou were made by Gaia to protect her, garou are very much creatures that can with no hyperbole be described as furry blenders. Garou were not made for humanity, they might see them as allies or family, but any garou born is born as a non-human. This is where the ST or other players need to really do their job, as the camera should at times portray garou from the eyes of regular people. Garou kill people, and I think often these people are made into bad people all ready to justify it to the players. But I have seen cool ideas of philodox going to cities and killing criminals for being criminals. I have been trying my damndest to remind people that cats and dogs are in fact wolf chow.<br /> <br /> But yeah, there not being mechanics to support this, combined with the inhumanity varying from writer to writer to a hilarious decree, does not really go into the monstrousness of them. For me, as someone who PREFERS playing non-homid garou, it can be annoying. Changeling actually did a MUCH better job at bringing the inhumanity to something useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T07:24:22-07:00","id":1194527,"title":"","content":"I understand, but that is not really what Im talking about. For most of the other gamelines, the different supernatural types are, by their nature monstrous, harmful to humanity, the world, reality, or something just because they exist, or to keep existing. Vampires have to feed and kill, for instance, in a very broad sense. To stave off the terror of eternity, they also have to do terrible things to stay sane.<br /> <br /> Werewolves/Garou, as a species do not have anything like that. They are not a curse or plague, but rather arguably truely perfectly natural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T07:43:33-07:00","id":1194530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194527#post1194527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolves/Garou, as a species do not have anything like that. They are not a curse or plague, but rather arguably truely perfectly natural.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that is the point of the game, garou are nature in cruelty and in compassion. Huge point is that it might not be the nature people -want-, bringing the horror. Trying to change this is such a radical setting hack that it would be better to just make your own creature.<br /> <br /> I mean, there would absolutely be room for non-garou werewolves that -are- harmful for the world in the setting, given garou are a species more than a mindset, parasite, curse/disease or whatnot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 03-12-2018, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T08:16:55-07:00","id":1194538,"title":"","content":"Not really. Someone mentioned transmitting lycanthrope through the bite rather than through hereditary means. Perhaps only humans and wolves bitten by a Garou in Frenzy become Garou, if they survive. Very little else has to change about the setting, but suddenly being Garou is just as much a calling as an affliction.<br /> <br /> The Garou population remains small, in order to repopulate, there is a significant chance they will murder the victim instead, and the only other option is Metis, (which adds a very interesting spin on Metis).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1721,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","user":"Beckett","date":". 03-12-2018, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T08:25:52-07:00","id":1194540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194538#post1194538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. Someone mentioned transmitting lycanthrope through the bite rather than through hereditary means. Very little else has to change about the setting, but suddenly being Garou is just as much a calling as an affliction.</div> </div> </div> </div>For homid garou, sure. But what about metis or lupus? If the garou do not have to watch out for breeding with one another, then their culture becomes a heck of a lot more insular as there is no need for kinfolk. If any canis can be bitten, would the BSDs (or even the Nation) start making shovelheads? What of the breeds of dog that are physically malformed?<br /> <br /> The difficulty of making new garou ties the race to keeping strong ties with humanity and wolves, denies them from breeding with one another and be constantly on the watch for new werewolves. If biting was an option, garou would be in a heck of a lot better situation than in the canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 03-12-2018, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T08:41:20-07:00","id":1194546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194538#post1194538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. Someone mentioned transmitting lycanthrope through the bite rather than through hereditary means. Perhaps only humans and wolves bitten by a Garou in Frenzy become Garou, if they survive. Very little else has to change about the setting, but suddenly being Garou is just as much a calling as an affliction.<br /> <br /> The Garou population remains small, in order to repopulate, there is a significant chance they will murder the victim instead, and the only other option is Metis, (which adds a very interesting spin on Metis).</div> </div> </div> </div>Why only in frenzy? Why only wolves? Why not dogs as well? How would the metis thing work, if the garou were never born garou? Why keep the numbers small, when you could go into a small town and frenzy and pick off the survivors to bolster your army? What about BSDs who would -gladly- take out a warehouse full of humans?<br /> <br /> I'm not trying to say that your idea is bad. I myself am trying to write an infectous werewolf species, so those are the thoughts that I have asked myself.<br /> <br /> Mind, the setting you describe all ready exist. It is an online game called Silver and Bone, which functions pretty much like that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T10:26:23-07:00","id":1194569,"title":"","content":"I got a few ideas..<br /> <br /> 1. Tweak the initiative system to allow characters who change declared actions at the usual -2 dice to have the option of interrupting a lesser initiative character or npc action as long as the interrupter had enough initiative to do so. This would give a better grasp on last minute body guarding or snatching items out of the air for fast paced craziness. Make clear that a round is about 3 or so seconds that way chracters that are thrown or have suffered some sort of dynamic are given due process. And it helps to point out use of supernatural speed or highlight really trained focus.<br /> <br /> 2. Make Pack Tactics a secondary skill that would lower the difficulty of actions taken by 1 for every other extra pack member involved in a maneuver for limited by the rank of the secondary ability. This would reward time and training invested invested to and simulate the power of the pack as opposed to the individual since this is how the Garou had a distinct advantage in the war of rage.<br /> <br /> 3. Ditch the kinfolk optional rank system and adopt the Kinfolk Status background.<br /> <br /> 4. Make Ronin rank a secondary citizen file system that brings them closer to being called into action and adopted by a tribe who begins to note and like what they are doing but to keep the idea of them being nothing without the actual Garou Nation make their highest rank gifts gained at x.5 that of the actual rank of the Ronin. So at rank 6 they can only reach a Lv.3 gift. This would push up play with players and give those character types a bit more than just a mercenary like feel as they are truly tying to get in to a tribe.<br /> <br /> 5. Create some secretive or more sinister places of power for other fera and evil strongholds for adversaries in more places than that are listed.<br /> <br /> 6. Make all Silent Strider Kinfolk possess the &quot;Gypsy Blood&quot; perk since Silent Strider Gypsies are all considered kinfolk. Would balance out the rather roaming presence of the tribe as a whole.<br /> <br /> 7. Make the older Silver Tolerance a 5 point merit since there is a 7 point Silver Immunity which ignores all effects.<br /> <br /> 8. Make it a rule that Rank 6 or greater characters can understand and maybe called by the one they serve to deal with an epic problem one of the Triat has decided the character capable to deal with. The difficulty should be immense.<br /> <br /> 9. Inform players on how to use the, &quot;Fade to Black&quot; system. In which you completely cover explicit scenes from younger, uncomfortable and immature players if need be. &quot;Ok she smiles at you and shoots a glance to twelve other Children of Gaia of alternate genders.. one metis has two genders and licks its lips. You move with them beyond the brush into a secluded spot where an older more experienced Theurge begins the ritual to subdue the pent up aggression within. Petting starts.. and from there my dear player your character experiences the sweet nectar of extasy as we FADE TO BLACK on this scene and move back to Monroe who is still at the store buying a Bone Gnawer a beer.&quot;<br /> <br /> 10. Create and alternate sect of Furies who have been infected with the Wyld Virus in mexico that have declared war and are no longer contagious.<br /> <br /> 11. Do more with the Siberak tribe strength and range as direct threats to the Spiral Dancers of nuclear sites in Russia. Leading for them to present themselves at a moot with the Garou nation.<br /> <br /> 12. Bring back the Gurps Werewolf the apocolypse fetishes and especially the silver sword.<br /> <br /> 13. List the Rite of Shadow Craft and the Craft Worker Merit use in the Uktena tribe book.<br /> <br /> 14. Restrict the &quot;Sorcerer&quot; Merit in WW20 to Doshi and Bubasti alone as their backgrounds explain how those cats sell some of the soul to get that kind of talent and the Kitsune using evil to fight evil as a purpose.. I mean c'mon... that's just tooo open. WAY too open. This Merit can justify doing what the cats and kitsune would normally do but make extraordinarily very, very easy for the character to do in almost no time or effort. I officially give a thumbs down on this merit being open to any other outside this selection.<br /> <br /> 15. Pure Ones should have far less difficulty dealing with spirits and the gauntlet of their native homeland.<br /> <br /> 16. Give Bone Gnawer an increased Kinfolk modifier in city or back water areas.<br /> <br /> 17. Buff up the new dream form characteristics for Mokole because the new ones ruined alot of combat value option that once made players truly fear them.<br /> <br /> 18. Make Naga poison unable to be soaked in any fashion. Resist Toxin and the like should only make the damage done by the poison have to be rolled.<br /> <br /> 19. Create more off planet threats that call Heros into action just before the Red star development.<br /> <br /> 20. Have background called &quot;Pack/Pride/Clutch/Murder etc..&quot; these represent a certain amount of npcs who have banned together with you to survive.<br /> <br /> 21. Because this makes more sense now a days. A long list for sits for players to use forums and or chat with other players for official New and Classic WoD content. (Edit: I meant Sites not sits.. ugh..)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23973-silentline","user":"Silentline","date":". 03-12-2018, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23973-silentline","name":"Silentline","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T13:45:42-07:00","id":1194621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194546#post1194546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why only in frenzy? Why only wolves? Why not dogs as well? How would the metis thing work, if the garou were never born garou? Why keep the numbers small, when you could go into a small town and frenzy and pick off the survivors to bolster your army? What about BSDs who would -gladly- take out a warehouse full of humans?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only in Frenzy because the intent is to make Garou monstrous without massivly rewriting the system. The Rage has to be very close to the surface to curse the victim, but 9 times out of 10, the Garou will either furry blender them to death or leave them hopelessly crippled that it is very difficult to increase Garou numbers, .<br /> <br /> BSD do not go around shovelheading entire towns because it draws way, way too much attention, devastates entire Wyrm powers in an area, and is too much work and wasted time to gain like 2 new Garou. And, to be honest, most BSD would probably be created by the Nation doing their normal antics on an innocent refinery and leaving a survivor or two, who sufdenly have really good reasons to hate the Nation well before Banes come to the scene.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194546#post1194546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind, the setting you describe all ready exist. It is an online game called Silver and Bone, which functions pretty much like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you might be confussed. Im not talking about making a new game with similar themes to WtA or anything. Im talking about a relatively minor singular change to the existing WtA game, without really changing anything else, (a few tweeks here and there to accomidate) to help WtA as a whole fit with the rest of the WoD. Again, in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1721,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","user":"Beckett","date":". 03-12-2018, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T13:59:16-07:00","id":1194624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194621#post1194621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only in Frenzy because the intent is to make Garou monstrous with massivly rewriting the system. The Rage has to be very close to the surface to curse the victim, but 9 times out of 10, the Garou will either furry blender them to death or leave them hopelessly crippled that it is very difficult to increase Garou numbers, .<br /> <br /> BSD do not go around shovelheading entire towns because it draws way, way too much attention, devastates entire Wyrm powers in an area, and is too much work and wasted time to gain like 2 new Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>What stops the garou from 'gaming' the system? Like, have your packmate frenzy and then pull the human out just in time and mother's touch them. One new garou, done. Better if you get the person you picked alone in a safe area to do this in. Plus, there is a merit called Berserkker which allows you to enter frenzy at will.<br /> <br /> With BSDs, they might even hold warehouse parties where the ones living get healed and inducted into the tribe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T14:12:59-07:00","id":1194626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194624#post1194624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What stops the garou from 'gaming' the system? Like, have your packmate frenzy and then pull the human out just in time and mother's touch them. One new garou, done. Better if you get the person you picked alone in a safe area to do this in. Plus, there is a merit called Berserkker which allows you to enter frenzy at will.<br /> <br /> With BSDs, they might even hold warehouse parties where the ones living get healed and inducted into the tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because its very dangerous to everyone involved. I mean, what stops a Camarilla Fledglings from Embracing a hundred people in one night and destroying every Kindred in the Domain the next?<br /> <br /> I mean, think about it a moment. If the bite version is used rather than the breeding one, it means that just about every single Garou out there is the &quot;lucky&quot; survivor of a brutal attack, likely one they can not fully remember or understand (delirium), because they where at the wrong place, and very likely resulted in their family or friends being killed, er, torn to shreds.<br /> <br /> Now, suddenly they are no longer human, having some sort of rage demon inside of them, (which might force them to do this to someone else at any time!!!). Their family feels strange around them, and even the family dog senses something is off. And the hallucinations. . .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1721,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","user":"Beckett","date":". 03-12-2018, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T14:15:09-07:00","id":1194627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194621#post1194621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you might be confussed. Im not talking about making a new game with similar themes to WtA or anything. Im talking about a relatively minor singular change to the existing WtA game, without really changing anything else, (a few tweeks here and there to accomidate) to help WtA as a whole fit with the rest of the WoD. Again, in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean that I have seen how a setting with werewolves with this ability function in practise and it is very hard to keep werewolf numbers low if you include the ability to transfer garou ability with a bite. The only reason garou are in such low numbers, is that they have to breed by traditional means. If they could frenzy bite (or regular bite like in the MET book), their numbers would rise because many garou would just go that route. Exactly what happened in the MET game.<br /> <br /> But it also means that there is more room for moral grayness among the garou, as all bitten might not join the Nation. If this was the case from the start, it might even mean there would be groups of werewolves that aren't Wyrmy, but are not heroes of Gaia either. Something which I think would fit in your WoD very well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194626#post1194626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because its very dangerous to everyone involved. I mean, what stops a Camarilla Fledglings from Embracing a hundred people in one night and destroying every Kindred in the Domain the next?</div> </div> </div> </div>Camarilla fledgings don't have a packmate that has an insta-heal ability as one of their rank 1 gifts, they don't have a totem that lets the packmates communicate by a mindlink. They don't have a culture of pack co-operation like the garou have. -A- camarilla fledging wouldn't be able to pull this off, no. But a pack that has been trained for this purpose and that has their sept's sanction? Heck yeah<br /> <br /> Plus, garou wouldn't be thinning their feeding stock by doing this, like vampires would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 03-12-2018, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T14:30:33-07:00","id":1194629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194627#post1194627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I mean that I have seen how a setting with werewolves with this ability function in practise and it is very hard to keep werewolf numbers low if you include the ability to transfer garou ability with a bite. The only reason garou are in such low numbers, is that they have to breed by traditional means. If they could frenzy bite (or regular bite like in the MET book), their numbers would rise because many garou would just go that route. Exactly what happened in the MET game.<br /> <br /> But it also means that there is more room for moral grayness among the garou, as all bitten might not join the Nation. If this was the case from the start, it might even mean there would be groups of werewolves that aren't Wyrmy, but are not heroes of Gaia either. Something which I think would fit in your WoD very well.</div> </div> </div> </div>If feel surviving a Frenzying Garou bite is insufficuent at keeping Garou numbers relatively similar, we could add something like the victim must also have been born under the same Auspice as the Garou biting them, or perhaps only Homid can infect humans, (both)?<br /> <br /> Looking back at my original post about the bite, it appears my edit specifying Crinos form and Berserker Frenzy didn't make it through, which might be adding confusion. To be clear, I am talking about replacing breeding as an option completely with repopulating Garou by the bite. The bite must be from a Crinos Garou in active Frenzy that does not kill or maim the victim, (who is not a Garou yet). The only other alternative is by two Garou creating a Metis, (well Skindancer Tribe), which is still very much against the Litany, and has it's own issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1721,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","user":"Beckett","date":". 03-12-2018, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T14:37:33-07:00","id":1194632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194629#post1194629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If feel surviving a Frenzying Garou bite is insufficuent at keeping Garou numbers relatively similar, we could add something like the victim must also have been born under the same Auspice as the Garou biting them, or perhaps only Homid can infect humans, (both)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would you want to keep the numbers similar, though? I mean, heck, having more werewolves gives room for more variety and therefore room for more monstrous werewolves. Plus more monstrous biting practises OUT of the need of warriors. Therefore, being a legit harm to humanity.<br /> <br /> EDIT: In terms of bite being breed specific, maybe only metis can transfer the curse, therefore keeping the garou numbers low as creating a metis would be harder in this setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 03-12-2018, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T14:48:57-07:00","id":1194636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194627#post1194627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Camarilla fledgings don't have a packmate that has an insta-heal ability as one of their rank 1 gifts, they don't have a totem that lets the packmates communicate by a mindlink. They don't have a culture of pack co-operation like the garou have. -A- camarilla fledging wouldn't be able to pull this off, no. But a pack that has been trained for this purpose and that has their sept's sanction? Heck yeah<br /> <br /> Plus, garou wouldn't be thinning their feeding stock by doing this, like vampires would.</div> </div> </div> </div>???<br /> A Fledgling can make an unlimited amount of other Cainites, really with no drawbacks. Presence is a thing, or they could just lie and say that as soon as all the other vampires are killed, we all turn back to humans, and everyone would probably believe them, (I mean, why not, it is a common vampire lore). <br /> <br /> It takes like 1 minute to drain and then Embrace someone. If someone wanted to game the system, they could easily Embrace a hundred vampires in a night, and it wouldn't take much to convince them to blitz Elyssium and destroy the &quot;evil&quot; Caintes the next to &quot;break the curse&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1721,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","user":"Beckett","date":". 03-12-2018, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T14:51:16-07:00","id":1194639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194480#post1194480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I respect your position, but painting the whole Nation by the Red Talon brush is still very misleading.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I suspect that painting Al Qaeda with the Mohammad Atta brush is misleading. I'd bet that some of that lot are against murdering innocent women and children and are in it because they hate U.S. foreign policy and truly believe that the West is genuinely trying to destroy Islam. John Rabe was a hard-core, dedicated Nazi, and yet he risked both his career as a diplomat and his life to save Chinese civilians during the Rape of Nanking.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut you can still make some generalizations about those groups. The Garou believe that human civilization is inherently corrupt and should be dismantled and aren't shy about using bloodshed. For every peaceful Child of Gaia, you've got a Shadow Lord, a Talon, a Get, and a Wendigo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T14:52:15-07:00","id":1194643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194629#post1194629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking back at my original post about the bite, it appears my edit specifying Crinos form and Berserker Frenzy didn't make it through, which might be adding confusion. To be clear, I am talking about replacing breeding as an option completely with repopulating Garou by the bite. The bite must be from a Crinos Garou in active Frenzy that does not kill or maim the victim, (who is not a Garou yet). The only other alternative is by two Garou creating a Metis, (well Skindancer Tribe), which is still very much against the Litany, and has it's own issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, a pack of rank 1 garou can easily game that situation to create more garou. Only things you need is a garou with the Berserkker merit, a theurge with Mother's Touch and packmates to hold the frenzying garou back once the bite has been done. Then the theurge can mother's touch the victim to save their life. Boom, done.<br /> <br /> Unlike the Camarilla, most tribes would have very little qualms in terms of not doing that, given it does not limit their source for feeding stock, can be done by a well trained pack relatively safely and would ensure more soldiers to the war MUCH easier than breeding with kinfolk and crossing your fingers that you got lucky. There is no need to keep a semblance of humanity, either, as garou do not have Humanity to uphold.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194636#post1194636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ???<br /> A Fledgling can make an unlimited amount of other Cainites, really with no drawbacks. Presence is a thing, or they could just lie and say that as soon as all the other vampires are killed, we all turn back to humans, and everyone would probably believe them, (I mean, why not, it is a common vampire lore).<br /> <br /> It takes like 1 minute to drain and then Embrace someone. If someone wanted to game the system, they could easily Embrace a hundred vampires in a night, and it wouldn't take much to convince them to blitz Elyssium and destroy the &quot;evil&quot; Caintes the next to &quot;break the curse&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but Camarilla would come calling if we were setting accurate. In WtA, not as much as the tribes absolutely positively -need- more warriors.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 03-12-2018, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T15:01:15-07:00","id":1194644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194639#post1194639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you can still make some generalizations about those groups. The Garou believe that human civilization is inherently corrupt and should be dismantled and aren't shy about using bloodshed. For every peaceful Child of Gaia, you've got a Shadow Lord, a Talon, a Get, and a Wendigo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only one of those tribes is without human kin, though. Wendigo TREASURE their kinfolk, so do the Fenrir. Shadow Lords would ensure their kinfolk would be in the best position, as would their allies. Basically, dismantling human civilization will not work as long as human kinfolk are a thing and lost cub of any tribe might pop up anywhere. Again, all the garou who want a new impegrium outside Red Talon are just blowing hot air, they cannot risk it. Not out of the goodness of their hearts, but because it would no longer be viable for them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T15:21:57-07:00","id":1194649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Silentline</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194569#post1194569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got a few ideas..<br /> <br /> 7. Make the older Silver Tolerance a 5 point merit since there is a 7 point Silver Immunity which ignores all effects.<br /> <br /> 12. Bring back the Gurps Werewolf the apocolypse fetishes and especially the silver sword.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>1. What book is silver immunity in? <br /> <br /> 2. I haven't read GURPS in FOREVER so I remember basiclaly nothing about it. (especially the fetishes). What was the silver sword? Was it different from a klaive?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T16:51:34-07:00","id":1194665,"title":"","content":"Admittedly Garou becoming Garou by more pop-culture interpretations of werewolves is interesting, but I don't really see how it makes the game fit more into the WoD. We already have a supernatural creature like that, and they're vampires (and despite attempts to show multiple view points on the origin of vampires, these divergent takes come off as clear falsehoods by bloodlines and sects being isolated from the epicenters of Cainite/Kindred society).<br /> <br /> There's simpler ways to introduce more of a morally grey setting. Aside from playing up tribal divisions, camp rivalry, general apathy versus fanaticism, and political corruption among the Nation, you can ramp up the much neglected Lunatic and non-criminal exiled Ronin (ripe for Skindancer recruitment!). Also play up more divergent philosophies on the nature of the Triat and Gaia; they've had such views sitting around in each of the core books since the early 90s. You could have the spirit order overall in disarray thanks to the increasing disconnect between the the physical and spiritual worlds, and spirits falling more and more into Triatic divisions. Introduce more tribal and regional specific interactions with the spirit world, use of ritual, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> One way I've come to view the conflict lately, to introduce a grayness to the cosmology itself, is looking at the Triat as parts of Gaia rather than alien entities invading her. The Wyld, the Weaver, and the Wyrm are her. SHE is the insane one. The cosmos itself is suffering from a self-destructive multiple personality disorder. Maybe the Garou and other Fera are fighting a war for what's increasingly a memory of a whole and functioning mother. Some Garou think killing all the Wyrmlings will return her to balance, or maybe its the Weaver that needs to be culled, or maybe the only way to forestall the Apocalypse would be an endless war of balancing these three aspects of her &quot;personality&quot;. The later fits in better with an animistic world view anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 03-12-2018, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T18:21:51-07:00","id":1194685,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of greater shades of gray in WW, though I wouldn't make a bite infect people. Instead I would place a greater focus on Tribal rivalries and difference in ideology between them.<br /> <br /> You could actually remove the Wyrm as the primary villain. Maybe it is the Weaver. That is more accurate to real world environmental issues - which result in large part from greater development. Then you have some Tribes who like the Weaver and modern technology while others want it destroyed. Some Tribes (or individual Garou) embrace the Wyrm as a destroyer, who will basically destroy human civilization and save the natural world. Of course, that would result in billions of human deaths, so some Garou object. <br /> <br /> Through in this diet of dynamic and the setting becomes very gray. The Wyrm is evil but it is also trying to save the natural world even if it means billions of human deaths. The Weaver has created a world where humans have a much higher standard of life than ever before - medicine, human rights, plentiful food and shelter, and so on. But in allowing humanity to thrive, the Weaver has allowed the rest of the natural world to come under threat.<br /> <br /> What will the Garou choose? It's not so obvious right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 03-12-2018, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T19:11:13-07:00","id":1194699,"title":"","content":"Lycanthropy caused by an existing werewolf biting you is mostly a function of the Universal horror movies. That is not how folklore depicts werewolves (or other people who change into different animals). That is almost always a form of witchcraft given to a person by the Devil or other evil entity. If someone really wants that as flavor text, the easiest fix is to simply have a Garou biting a pre-Changer in order to awaken the beast or otherwise provoke a change that might not happen otherwise. In my games, it is a common occurrence with Lost Cubs or even Lunatics.<br /> <br /> Most stories that one could tell with a cursed transmission of lycanthropy can already be told by emphasizing existing concepts like Lost Cubs, Lunatics, and Ronin. After first edition, the game really played down those aspects as part of the setting, and I think it was a mistake as those kinds of concepts are what most people, unfamiliar with the WoD version, think of. The WtA lore we know can be a big obstacle for people who might be curious about a werewolf game, but then don't think what the game describes is anything they're familiar with. It's one reason in my own chronicles, I increase the population of Ronin considerably (and most Ronin are not exiles from Garou society, but werewolves who've never entered Garou society, either being by themselves or part of existing Ronin groups who seek a cure for their &quot;disease&quot;) and heavily utilize both Lost Cubs and Lunatics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T20:07:20-07:00","id":1194710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194699#post1194699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most stories that one could tell with a cursed transmission of lycanthropy can already be told by emphasizing existing concepts like Lost Cubs, Lunatics, and Ronin. After first edition, the game really played down those aspects as part of the setting, and I think it was a mistake as those kinds of concepts are what most people, unfamiliar with the WoD version, think of. The WtA lore we know can be a big obstacle for people who might be curious about a werewolf game, but then don't think what the game describes is anything they're familiar with. It's one reason in my own chronicles, I increase the population of Ronin considerably (and most Ronin are not exiles from Garou society, but werewolves who've never entered Garou society, either being by themselves or part of existing Ronin groups who seek a cure for their &quot;disease&quot;) and heavily utilize both Lost Cubs and Lunatics.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the reason why I'm so eager for Storytellers' Vault to approve WtA templates, so that I could publish stuff about these garou. The Currs who seek to dismantle the Nation, the Curers who seek to cure their condition and the various sub-groups of garou who have changed without knowledge of the Nation. Or ones that reject their religion/ways and seek their own roads.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T20:42:41-07:00","id":1194721,"title":"","content":"Yeah WtA really neglected its outcasts. It was never on the level of Mage, nor would it need to, but even Vampire got more love with the Thinblood and far flung bloodlines. It would be nice to have an updated look at ronin, more on the Curs and Skindancers (even the little tribes not part of the Nation would be nice too), and for them to really delve into Lost Cubs and Lunatics.<br /> <br /> There's lots I love in what Revised and W20 did for the game, but it really lost that sense of social disintegration that just oozed from the older books I've read (despite early installment weirdness).<br /> <br /> At the same time, I'm also tired of the calls to make the Garou more monstress. They can be pretty bad already raw by most standards, and it's something I've found myself having to defend the game against. Making everyone into asshole and everything darker does not make a setting deeper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 03-13-2018, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T15:09:09-07:00","id":1194994,"title":"","content":"I ended up importing the Ghost Wolves from Forsaken into my W:tA setting, as those who undergo all the training and rites to master their new forms and take on their Auspice role, but who either fail at or just refuse to take the tribal rite of passage. Werewolves on the fringes of the Garou Nation who aren't outcasts or litany criminals the way ronin are presumed to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T21:39:44-07:00","id":1195121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194721#post1194721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah WtA really neglected its outcasts. It was never on the level of Mage, nor would it need to, but even Vampire got more love with the Thinblood and far flung bloodlines. It would be nice to have an updated look at ronin, more on the Curs and Skindancers (even the little tribes not part of the Nation would be nice too), and for them to really delve into Lost Cubs and Lunatics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think one reason for that is unlike any outcasts in the other games (like Caitiffs or Anarchs in Vampires, or various Orphans in Mage), there was a mechanical factor that prevented werewolves from gaining power if they were outsiders - the need for renown to get rank so you can get more powerful Gifts. A PC who went down that route was giving up a lot of cool stuff in a way that Caitiffs never did.<br /> <br /> Also, one could imagine a group of anarchs or other loner vampires avoiding the Prince and his court and Camarilla society, yet those PCs could still have lots of fun doing stuff and still interacting with other vampires. It was much harder for a group of ronin to do so - the ostracism was too strong. Or the attraction to join the Nation and accept everything about it was too strong so the concept wouldn't last. It'd take a lot more work for the ST to integrate those PCs into a setting in the way a Vampire or Mage ST did not have to do with a similar group of PCs. I think it's entirely possible to do that, but some adjustments are needed. Having a good setting book, which takes some NPC ronin or Lost Cubs or Lunatics (not that these last two would be models for PCs, unless you're talking strictly backstory inspiration) and set them up in that situation for a model for the readers, would have helped that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T23:27:22-07:00","id":1195152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194994#post1194994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ended up importing the Ghost Wolves from Forsaken into my W:tA setting, as those who undergo all the training and rites to master their new forms and take on their Auspice role, but who either fail at or just refuse to take the tribal rite of passage. Werewolves on the fringes of the Garou Nation who aren't outcasts or litany criminals the way ronin are presumed to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did pretty much the same thing... tribeless Garou = ghost wolves. My motivation was that the term 'ronin' felt kinda anachronistic, since Japan is closed off and relatively unknown in the 1840s. Borrowing words for them to use in common werewolf parlance just seemed odd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T01:49:54-07:00","id":1195182,"title":"","content":"Before Vampire 5th the Camarilla was seeing itself as responsible for all vampires. Ergo even obscure bloodlines and such were in their domain of government and therefore integrated into society, even if ouseted or living on the fringe of the kainite society.<br /> <br /> Garou live isn't this way. Tolerance for werewolves lifing within the protectorate of a garou sept, without adhereing to the duties of the garou as a people is low. Sure, any sept might tolerate a lone Stargazer in their protectorate, for they serve Gaia in some way one doesn't understand, and sure the lone Glass Walker or Bone Gnawer in the human community might also be tolerated. A Ronin, actively denying the very way of life of the garou however....<br /> Someone like this is driven away, possibly killed in the process, for he is a heretic and without right to live as a parasite within the sept's protectorate...<br /> <br /> So, Ronin as players don't fit into a game that well.<br /> Having a game of 100% Ronin characters, is a different topic, but it ain't werewolf in most parts of the game...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T03:55:23-07:00","id":1195210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1194721#post1194721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the same time, I'm also tired of the calls to make the Garou more monstress. They can be pretty bad already raw by most standards, and it's something I've found myself having to defend the game against. Making everyone into asshole and everything darker does not make a setting deeper.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am very sympathetic towards those who do not want to play a more regular werewolf, but yeah. Garou are an animistic species that is tasked by their earth mother into protecting the earth. They function like they do because it makes the most sense. Invoking the bite will automaticly changes just how the whole rigmarole of breeding is done and a lot of garou are not above spreading the blood if they could. Plus, my favourite part of the setting is that garou are not limited to just human-borns, so the bite thing to me would take away some of the best parts of the setting.<br /> <br /> This is why, when I am talking about traditional (western) werewolves, I'd like them to be a separate specie entirely. Not only would it free it to be modified more and developed into its own thing, but they could easily contrast the garou in how they function.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1195121#post1195121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think one reason for that is unlike any outcasts in the other games (like Caitiffs or Anarchs in Vampires, or various Orphans in Mage), there was a mechanical factor that prevented werewolves from gaining power if they were outsiders - the need for renown to get rank so you can get more powerful Gifts. A PC who went down that route was giving up a lot of cool stuff in a way that Caitiffs never did.<br /> <br /> Also, one could imagine a group of anarchs or other loner vampires avoiding the Prince and his court and Camarilla society, yet those PCs could still have lots of fun doing stuff and still interacting with other vampires. It was much harder for a group of ronin to do so - the ostracism was too strong. Or the attraction to join the Nation and accept everything about it was too strong so the concept wouldn't last. It'd take a lot more work for the ST to integrate those PCs into a setting in the way a Vampire or Mage ST did not have to do with a similar group of PCs. I think it's entirely possible to do that, but some adjustments are needed. Having a good setting book, which takes some NPC ronin or Lost Cubs or Lunatics (not that these last two would be models for PCs, unless you're talking strictly backstory inspiration) and set them up in that situation for a model for the readers, would have helped that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the more I look at Forsaken, the more I see solutions to these very issues. In forsaken, there are Lodges for this purpose. Even if you are tribeless, you still get cool stuff from the lodge. I think WtA would benefit from having lodges of non-aligned garou, to showcase how they live compared to the Nation.<br /> <br /> Plus, it would give nice buffer room to have between Gaians and BSDs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T05:20:01-07:00","id":1195231,"title":"","content":"But would it really improve WtA and the themes the game is about ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T07:26:46-07:00","id":1195288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1195231#post1195231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But would it really improve WtA and the themes the game is about ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The former, creating a new shifter specie to match a more traditional werewolf, would mean those who want to play that would, rather than trying to make garou into one.<br /> <br /> The latter would offer the setting and the world a bit of variation in how garou can differ outside the tribes. Both would, in my opinion, aid WtA's themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T09:54:51-07:00","id":1195341,"title":"","content":"-<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz\">CeltSPZ</a></b>- The Silver sword (let me think here.. um) Lv.4 Gnosis 8 or something (shrug) I know I had complaints about its gnosis level that day. This fetish which seemed like an overglorified Silver Broadsword but it was much easier to create than the Regal Klaive and would fit in a trench or long coat. At this time I had access to old Gurps books of which I did not own. This time period was back in the day when I was new to were-wolf and had a strict storyteller who we had to bargain with just to get my character a ring to start with. Would be nice to see that list of fetishes added to the newer one.<br /> <br /> As for the Silver Immunity Merit I don't know why I even wrote that it doesn't exist and if it does I cant recall it. The proper post was supposed to be &quot;7. Make the older merit Silver Tolerance a 5 point merit since there should be a 7 point Silver Immunity which ignores all effects associated to silver and TRULY special to its price balance. You might as well have an all the way version. Besides a well placed super heated attack at Difficulty 9 to soak usually ends most characters anyhow as does terminal velocity at 300+ feet among other things. I've never found it hard to balance things out with a player who wanted silver Tolerance but I do have a rule of it being limited to one character per story<br /> line.<br /> <br /> -<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe\">Onkwe</a>- The Ronin stand point is a well crafted one. Just needs to be more to it. The skirmishes to prove worth are sometimes the best ones.</b><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23973-silentline","name":"Silentline","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T10:31:15-07:00","id":1195361,"title":"","content":"The contradictory system for ronin doesn't help in having full filling outcast games, along with what exactly is renown.<br /> <br /> Starting with ronin themselves, it says in 'Pariahs: Guide to Outcasts' and implies in the core books of 1st, 2nd, and Revised that ronin have no rank. That's fine, but it doesn't present a system in how they earn further gifts, even though they can. Does this mean ronin can learn pretty much any gift then, regardless of rank, if they can convince a Garou or spirit that has access to them to teach/grant it? Then it says in Rite of the Lone Wolf that they simply lose tribal membership and only temporary renown they've accumulated up to that point, but they can in theory still advance themselves mechanically as any Garou. However in W20 it says ronin are now rank 0, which puts us back in the nebulous system mentioned before. On top of these systems, the ronin section in Pariahs makes a distinction between criminal outcasts and those who willingly leave for various reasons (penance, harano, etc.); such as the later can keep their name and tend to be more pitied and somewhat acknowledged unlike the exiled convict variety.<br /> <br /> This brings us back to the issues of renown. In WtA it's never made clear if renown is purely a social system established by the Nation or if its something more related to the Garou's relationship to the Umbra (unless W20 or some sourcebook I've never read clears this up). At times it seems like it could be either. I figured it has to do with their connection to their tribal totems, which backs up of their status in relationship to Gaian spirits and why they teach certain levels of gifts based off rank. Otherwise I don't see why spirits would bother acknowledging something so rigid that was purely a social constructed system by the Garou. Being outside this relationship then makes sense why outcasts would be on the outs and not trusted by spirits, along with how how the minor tribes outside of the Nation can function more or less as the big tribes (or BSDs in relationship to the Wyrm). It's why I like Forsaken being very upfront about what exactly renown is in relationship to Uratha society and the Spirit world.<br /> <br /> This is why I think a system for outcasts needs to have an update. Certainly most of the perks should go to those being a part of the Nation or at least part of a tribe or some kind of entity aligned with a totem spirit, but there should be a greater exploration of a system for those operating outside them. If renown is a part of being attached to a greater spirit, maybe a ronin who has a personal totem spirit can be vouched for to a lesser degree in dealing with spirits. Maybe those who voluntarily leave, but are still more or less loyal to the Nation, are more like Forsaken's Ghost Wolves. This could also help with those who maybe want to play a Lost Club that never joined Garou society, opening the game up to more varied style of play without fundamentally altering the core of what WtA is about.<br /> <br /> And yeah I think the term 'ronin' itself should not be its official designation. It works fine as a slang term, but I do prefer something like Ghost Wolf or the older canon term of Lone Wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 03-14-2018, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T10:31:50-07:00","id":1195363,"title":"","content":"Here's a scan of the Silver Sword from the GURPS book;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/EcBOYtV\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/EcBOYtV\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/EcBOYtV\" target=\"_blank\"> https://imgur.com/EcBOYtV </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T13:58:46-07:00","id":1195460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1195210#post1195210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am very sympathetic towards those who do not want to play a more regular werewolf, but yeah. Garou are an animistic species that is tasked by their earth mother into protecting the earth. They function like they do because it makes the most sense. Invoking the bite will automaticly changes just how the whole rigmarole of breeding is done and a lot of garou are not above spreading the blood if they could. Plus, my favourite part of the setting is that garou are not limited to just human-borns, so the bite thing to me would take away some of the best parts of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Instead of lycanthropy being a transmissible curse, couldn't there be a rite or gift that allows for a Garou to bite a lost cub or lunatic and fully awaken their Garou heritage? It isn't like the bite actually turns the individual into a werewolf, it just awakens something that was within them all along... a more violent and active 'baptism of fire.' That solves the problem of 'werewolf plagues' were frenzies result in lots of newly infected fera, but allows for the bite to still be part of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T17:28:13-07:00","id":1195540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1195152#post1195152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did pretty much the same thing... tribeless Garou = ghost wolves. My motivation was that the term 'ronin' felt kinda anachronistic, since Japan is closed off and relatively unknown in the 1840s. Borrowing words for them to use in common werewolf parlance just seemed odd.</div> </div> </div> </div>I went with &quot;Outcasts&quot; for the longest time, mostly just because of the old WoD book about caitiff, ronin and orphans. That and I was using the term pariahs for something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T20:41:14-07:00","id":1195601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1195152#post1195152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did pretty much the same thing... tribeless Garou = ghost wolves. My motivation was that the term 'ronin' felt kinda anachronistic, since Japan is closed off and relatively unknown in the 1840s. Borrowing words for them to use in common werewolf parlance just seemed odd.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my games, I use the term &quot;vargr&quot; (or warg/worg if you prefer) for most of what the setting calls ronin, and only use the term ronin for the &quot;hired guns&quot; attempting to get back into a sept and tribe by doing the dirty jobs. Since vargr actually means wolf, and has also had a meaning of &quot;outlaw&quot; I think it well describes those werewolves who live outside Garou society.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T20:52:07-07:00","id":1195603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1195361#post1195361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why I think a system for outcasts needs to have an update. Certainly most of the perks should go to those being a part of the Nation or at least part of a tribe or some kind of entity aligned with a totem spirit, but there should be a greater exploration of a system for those operating outside them. If renown is a part of being attached to a greater spirit, maybe a ronin who has a personal totem spirit can be vouched for to a lesser degree in dealing with spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I'm thinking a discussion of ronin (and to a lesser degree lost cubs and lunatics) and how they live and operate outside the Garou Nation should have a thread all its own. That way we can brainstorm ideas of not only how to make them a larger part of the setting, but also the ways it can be viable for ronin PCs to be played in a game, whether as an entire group or perhaps even as part of a PC party with more traditional Garou (although perhaps not as part of a pack).<br /> <br /> We could discuss their relations with spirits, alternatives to renown, how they might learn Gifts, and how they might be organized into societies, lodges, sects, etc.<br /> <br /> I'll have to do some thinking before I'd start a thread myself, but I'd certainly contribute if someone else is already raring to go and posts the first thread.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T03:01:17-07:00","id":1195667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1195288#post1195288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The former, creating a new shifter specie to match a more traditional werewolf, would mean those who want to play that would, rather than trying to make garou into one.<br /> <br /> The latter would offer the setting and the world a bit of variation in how garou can differ outside the tribes. Both would, in my opinion, aid WtA's themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I would think, that the game would suffer, much like the core theme of Vampire, the personal horror and loss of humanity, suffered with the introduction of new shiny stuff like bloodlines, Roads and so on.<br /> <br /> If one wanted to play Werewolf's within a looser Setting, possibly colser to legends one might know, then CoD Forsaken or Changing Breeds would be suitable, or if you can get it &quot;Everlasting&quot;. <br /> <br /> <br /> It is okay to play WtA a different way, of course, especially if one has played the core game for a long time and is saturated by it's motives and themes. But I feel to make the Setting that open to begin with is a bad idea, for it will distract from the elemental mature theme of Savage Horror the game is about at it's core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T08:21:58-07:00","id":1195731,"title":"","content":"Ana &lt;----- You are a GOD. THANK YOU!!! The only copy of it I've seen in recent was a low grade version listed on a character in stargazers tibet character descripts which does it no<br /> justice. I havn't seen this descript in so many years.<br /> <br /> Do you have the full list? Please tell me you do! At this point if you don't have the full list just lie to me to make me happy! I'm already geeked out by the Silver sword post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23973-silentline","user":"Silentline","date":"Edit: ......Teach them oh veteran players......For they do not know the POWER of the Gurps side..... -.- ) 03-15-2018, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23973-silentline","name":"Silentline","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T14:25:51-07:00","id":1195846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1195667#post1195667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I would think, that the game would suffer, much like the core theme of Vampire, the personal horror and loss of humanity, suffered with the introduction of new shiny stuff like bloodlines, Roads and so on.<br /> <br /> If one wanted to play Werewolf's within a looser Setting, possibly colser to legends one might know, then CoD Forsaken or Changing Breeds would be suitable, or if you can get it &quot;Everlasting&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> It is okay to play WtA a different way, of course, especially if one has played the core game for a long time and is saturated by it's motives and themes. But I feel to make the Setting that open to begin with is a bad idea, for it will distract from the elemental mature theme of Savage Horror the game is about at it's core.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason why I am being the Devil's Avocate so much here, is that the game is called Werewolf the Apocalypse in a setting where typically the species are modified, but still are at their core what it says on the tin.<br /> <br /> What people possibly expect from a werewolf-game is a game of dealing with the ferocious predator and the human having to share mental space with it. It means dreading every full moon, losing control and leaving behind carnage. It also can mean dealing with themes of cannibalism and isolation. Basically, a game about monsters.<br /> <br /> <br /> That is not WtA, even though Rage is there it is harnessed to protect and losing control is generally seen as a very bad thing. The focus isn't on the duality of man and the monster, but on humanity and the wilderness. Plus the whole spiritualism that comes with WtA, which is a great portrayal of animism.<br /> <br /> <br /> To be honest, those two aren't really similar. I have looked around and played in games that are werewolf games without WtA, and the themes truly are vastly different.<br /> <br /> <br /> But I agree, using Forsaken Chronicler's Guide would be the best bet for those who want to play traditional werewolves. One thing I like about CoD is that it has a very loose cosmology. But to be fair, if you don't know the setting, picking up a RPG about werewolves and not getting the traditional werewolf story CAN put people off.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23973-silentline\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23973_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23973\" data-vbnamecard=\"23973\">Silentline</a> I actually own the physical book, though mostly to have it than anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T04:14:40-07:00","id":1196007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1195846#post1195846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What people possibly expect from a werewolf-game is a game of dealing with the ferocious predator and the human having to share mental space with it. It means dreading every full moon, losing control and leaving behind carnage. It also can mean dealing with themes of cannibalism and isolation. Basically, a game about monsters.<br /> <br /> That is not WtA, even though Rage is there it is harnessed to protect and losing control is generally seen as a very bad thing. The focus isn't on the duality of man and the monster, but on humanity and the wilderness. Plus the whole spiritualism that comes with WtA, which is a great portrayal of animism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, isn't that something that depends on the troupe and the ST's choice of plot and the ST's choice of when to enforce what roll ?<br /> <br /> Personally the rage difficulty with the current moon phase is a hinderance to my style as ST. Frenzies come too often at points that don't suit the story. Also, it is when Moots are, and garou meet. Cool theme for the Revel, not so much for the other Moot parts, and only the Get TB has a Rite to smooth the problem that all the Rage monsters are at the same place.<br /> <br /> On the other hand I'm a huge fan of 2nd Editons long term Curse effects. Rolling Rage against Willpower every month and if the Rage wins, come up with some incident that destroys or at least throws back the garou's attempt to have a human-like life. You get angry and while not killing someone, your partner truly sees the monster in you, and decides she not sleep on the couch. Or your neighbour starts to sense your rage and starts to oust you from all neighbourhood activities. <br /> <br /> Sure, you can run WtA as a eco-terrorist save the world from supernatural destruction setting, with huge plots and packs of PCs that travel from sept to sept having adventures every day of their live. Or you can have the PCs live in a sept. Have friends, a live, downtime, and the occasional supernatural wyrm threat, that isn't just attacked and moved on from, but need investigation, observation, then the executed attack and then the aftermath. And all that at the expanse of the human connections the garou has.<br /> <br /> Surely, it depends on the consensus the troupe hopefully has, on what their game should be about.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T11:25:26-07:00","id":1196140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1196007#post1196007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, isn't that something that depends on the troupe and the ST's choice of plot and the ST's choice of when to enforce what roll ?<br /> <br /> Personally the rage difficulty with the current moon phase is a hinderance to my style as ST. Frenzies come too often at points that don't suit the story. Also, it is when Moots are, and garou meet. Cool theme for the Revel, not so much for the other Moot parts, and only the Get TB has a Rite to smooth the problem that all the Rage monsters are at the same place.<br /> <br /> On the other hand I'm a huge fan of 2nd Editons long term Curse effects. Rolling Rage against Willpower every month and if the Rage wins, come up with some incident that destroys or at least throws back the garou's attempt to have a human-like life. You get angry and while not killing someone, your partner truly sees the monster in you, and decides she not sleep on the couch. Or your neighbour starts to sense your rage and starts to oust you from all neighbourhood activities.<br /> <br /> Sure, you can run WtA as a eco-terrorist save the world from supernatural destruction setting, with huge plots and packs of PCs that travel from sept to sept having adventures every day of their live. Or you can have the PCs live in a sept. Have friends, a live, downtime, and the occasional supernatural wyrm threat, that isn't just attacked and moved on from, but need investigation, observation, then the executed attack and then the aftermath. And all that at the expanse of the human connections the garou has.<br /> <br /> Surely, it depends on the consensus the troupe hopefully has, on what their game should be about.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, that even the low-key sept-life game might not be what a werewolf-fan seeks in a game titled werewolf. For one, the low-grade game WITH the 2nd ed Rage rule you mentioned still has the players accept these truths about the setting;<ul><li><i>* Werewolves change when they want to, change being mostly a non.emotion tied thing.</i></li> <li><i>* Werewolves live in a quasi-militaritic commune that has strict rules and is highly political and established.</i></li> <li><i>* Werewolves can freely enter the spirit world and are part spirit themselves. They also have 'classes' decided by the moon.</i></li> <li><i>* Werewolves get, from the outset, 5 forms to use and don't have to earn any of them through deeds.</i></li> <li><i>* Being a werewolf is not a moral-quandry by mechanics, as you always were one.</i></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> That, to me, takes the WtA setting very far from the general conseous of werewolf games I have seen done by people who aren't influenced by WtA at all. Here are some things found in these games to contrast the above list;<ul><li><i>* Werewolves can learn to change at will, but only after dedicating time to accepting the change. Even then, it often is extremely painful and takes a long time to change until higher experience levels.</i></li> <li><i>* Werewolves may live in packs or they may not. Even if they do live in packs, things are rarely very strictly set up and new packs/cultures pop up a lot. Global cultures are either non-existent or very rare.</i></li> <li><i>* Werewolves may be spiritual, but they aren't any more likely to enter the spirit world as humans. Or they might just not be spiritual at all.</i></li> <li><i>* Any form outside the 'werewolf' form has to be earned through wanting to have it, otherwise werewolves are stuck with two forms.</i></li> <li><i>* Being a werewolf can mean that you have two different minds in your head, your human and your wolf. They may not even communicate at all, if you deny your wolf nature.</i></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> The above is only one type of Werewolf RP versions I have seen, but even its social RP purpose structure differs from WtA immensely and makes the garou look like super soldiers compared to the werewolves these RPs present. This is important, because if you do not want to play the game of those supersoldiers, WtA is not a werewolf game you'd like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T16:37:12-07:00","id":1196277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1195603#post1195603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now I'm thinking a discussion of ronin (and to a lesser degree lost cubs and lunatics) and how they live and operate outside the Garou Nation should have a thread all its own. That way we can brainstorm ideas of not only how to make them a larger part of the setting, but also the ways it can be viable for ronin PCs to be played in a game, whether as an entire group or perhaps even as part of a PC party with more traditional Garou (although perhaps not as part of a pack).<br /> <br /> We could discuss their relations with spirits, alternatives to renown, how they might learn Gifts, and how they might be organized into societies, lodges, sects, etc.<br /> <br /> I'll have to do some thinking before I'd start a thread myself, but I'd certainly contribute if someone else is already raring to go and posts the first thread.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I'll post the thread this weekend and sum up what was discussed here already in the first post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T01:27:20-07:00","id":1197518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1196140#post1196140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That, to me, takes the WtA setting very far from the general conseous of werewolf games I have seen done by people who aren't influenced by WtA at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I can imagine, although I can't really name any setting where these aspects are as you describe.<br /> <br /> I guess with Everlasting or the Dresden Files RPG such setups are possible, but these games aren't werewolf-centered normally.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T03:11:13-07:00","id":1197538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1197518#post1197518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I can imagine, although I can't really name any setting where these aspects are as you describe.<br /> <br /> I guess with Everlasting or the Dresden Files RPG such setups are possible, but these games aren't werewolf-centered normally.</div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't any published games, more online games that people have made. But those elements are a very common thread in them. Then there are takes of werewolves that are <a href=\"http://werewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Werewolf_(Species)#Types_of_Werewolves\" target=\"_blank\">like this.</a><br /> <br /> My point is, that garou are very different from how werewolves are generally seen and though werewolves differ from setting to setting, garou generally take the concept of a werewolf so far that they resemble a fantasy race than a condition a person gains.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T17:37:12-07:00","id":1197797,"title":"","content":"I was reading Beast the Primordial, and it was giving me some cool ideas for using fomori in new ways. You could bring in a more cerebral element in regards to adapting lairs as mini-umbral realms, interlinked fomori families on a more spiritual level, and even possibly 'wyrm propaganda' by adapting what Beasts believe to be their purpose.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T04:00:54-07:00","id":1197930,"title":"","content":"One thing that I -seriously- do want to change, and which matters to me a lot as a fan of WtA as a complex entity, is addressing Red Talons as a whole. One of the bigger issues I have with the MET book is how it did not change the tribe in a way that would make them more playable for a wider range of people. Instead, they all but painted devil horns and pitchforks on them. Enough that I think the -actual- demons in cWoD would be horrified.<br /> <br /> As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3506_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3506\" data-vbnamecard=\"3506\">Uniform Two Six</a> has multiple times pointed out, some Red Talons eat babies. This is very much a known thing in the Nation, enough that the garou actually -joke- about it. The Red Talons even have rites to avoid big renown losses for the act.<br /> <br /> So, let us actually address this in-setting. Have Judges of Doom get tired of the jokes and do an in-depth investigation of the whole thing. Have them put the tribe on trial and have setting wide consequences for the Talons.<br /> <br /> I would be happy if the tribe was cast out/destroyed from the Nation. Or remade. Regardless, I highly doubt it would affect many games, given how Talons are usually treated in-setting and out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 03-21-2018, 07:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T14:37:50-07:00","id":1198127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1197930#post1197930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Have them put the tribe on trial and have setting wide consequences for the Talons.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet for all of the overtly evil stuff, the Red Talons make useful -- even loyal -- allies. There's a great point made in a sidebar somewhere that Wyrm-Taint is emphatically <i>not</i> synonymous with evil. The Talons are not (generally) Wyrm-Tainted, even though a great many of them are pretty evil. But the same could be said for the Shadow Lords. In the Child of Gaia Tribebook, the point gets made that if the Shadow Lords (and presumably the Talons too) are so evil, why doesn't the Nation do something about them. The answer is that they have proven themselves time and again to be powerful allies who can get results -- regardless of the means. Changing the relationship between the Talons and the rest of the Nation, would fundamentally change W:tA, and <i>not</i> for the better. One of the developers made a statement in a little editorial at the end of one of the books that every now and then you need to just stop using the term &quot;Garou&quot; and substitute &quot;werewolf&quot; instead. The Garou can be noble and generous -- but they're still werewolves. Because they're <i>Garou</i> they are touched upon by human morality. Because they are <i>werewolves</i> they are not bound by it.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe characters should have allies whom they wouldn't want to allow within a Texas-Mile of their friends and families. But they must remain their allies, because their enemy is somehow <i>worse</i>. <i>That's</i> the World of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 03-21-2018, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T15:23:50-07:00","id":1198145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1198127#post1198127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet for all of the overtly evil stuff, the Red Talons make useful -- even loyal -- allies. There's a great point made in a sidebar somewhere that Wyrm-Taint is emphatically <i>not</i> synonymous with evil. The Talons are not (generally) Wyrm-Tainted, even though a great many of them are pretty evil. But the same could be said for the Shadow Lords. In the Child of Gaia Tribebook, the point gets made that if the Shadow Lords (and presumably the Talons too) are so evil, why doesn't the Nation do something about them. The answer is that they have proven themselves time and again to be powerful allies who can get results -- regardless of the means. Changing the relationship between the Talons and the rest of the Nation, would fundamentally change W:tA, and <i>not</i> for the better. One of the developers made a statement in a little editorial at the end of one of the books that every now and then you need to just stop using the term &quot;Garou&quot; and substitute &quot;werewolf&quot; instead. The Garou can be noble and generous -- but they're still werewolves. Because they're <i>Garou</i> they are touched upon by human morality. Because they are <i>werewolves</i> they are not bound by it.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe characters should have allies whom they wouldn't want to allow within a Texas-Mile of their friends and families. But they must remain their allies, because their enemy is somehow <i>worse</i>. <i>That's</i> the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference there is, that people still want to play Shadow Lords and see them as interesting. But Red Talons are seen as distruptive, extremely hard to play (if not impossible according to some), mere monsters or if you actually get someone playing one, arguing with Elders because human thing not right. It is not an issue of them being evil and horrible in-universe as much as it is an issue of the tribe being stereotyped or banned. Not due to the content of their tribe, because I have yet to see the Shadow Lord tribe banned from a game. But because to most, a Talon character is nothing more than one that argues with everyone, is hard to understand and can ruin the game.<br /> <br /> As much as this can be blamed on bad players, there is the truth that if the tribe cannot be seen or even considered by anyone as something worth trying to play, there is a problem. This is why the changes in the MET book, making the tribe openly ally with torturers and gain highly increased numbers yet be even more angry, was such a waste for me. A huge part of the Talons belief is that humanity is cruel for torturing and hurting Gaia, as such they kill cleanly. Dying Cubs torturing humans for Gaia is an antithesis to the Talon way. Yet they are now accepted openly. Instead of the writers working on making the tribe easier to play.<br /> <br /> Outside that, I don't myself mind Talons being what they are. I like that they are ignorant of their humanity at parts, I like that they justify to themselves the human killing and I like their culture based on a more primitive way of life. But that is not what most people ever get to see, they see only the human eating Rage ball #345. No matter how cool a concept the Talons are, if getting that interesting stuff in play is hard, then the concept has to be fixed to work better.<br /> <br /> And, again, the issue isn't that Talons hate humanity and don't care about human lives. Shadow Lord and Silver Fang characters do that too and much worse things. The issue is that to play a Red Talon outside a Talon-only game, you have to make so many concensions and even then you are damn lucky if the group's STs even allow them. In addition, most Talon PCs often end up generally seen as boring rageballs that just argue and no one understands them. Poigant, but that burns out the Talon players and the other players to the Talons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T18:15:59-07:00","id":1198195,"title":"","content":"I would just ignore the pointlessly edgy BS canon Talons do. This doesn't mean ditching the darker aspects of where the themes of the tribe can go, but like with many of the 'asshole' tribes, there was little nuance built into them. The Talons could be a very fascinating exploration of how might animals act if they had the same sense of consciousness and sentience human beings and a few other species on our planet possess, and the hatred and alienation they might feel at being driven into near extinction for the sake of 'human progress', not to mention even among their fellow Garou as homids and metis dominate the other tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T19:08:01-07:00","id":1198204,"title":"","content":"As I've advocated before, I think the Red Talons should be refocused as the &quot;overly Wyld&quot; Tribe as a foil for the &quot;overly Weaver&quot; Tribe in the Glasswalkers. Rather than a far too human hatred of humans for the most lupus dominated Tribe, you can keep a lot of their darker aspects without the BS if they've decided that the only way to rebalance the Triat is to spread the Wyld without fear of consequence. Instead of being obsessed with the past and lost, since animals were going extinct without humans doing anything, they anger and alienation gets channeled into bringing new things into the world. Disease, species of pests, crazy hybrids of existing predators suddenly appearing. Humans will survive or perish by the laws of nature, as new things evolve under the Wyld's energetic fury to challenge humanity for dominance of the land.<br /> <br /> It's a bit Ratkin, sure, but hardly the only Tribe to overlap with a Fera, and the Talons would still be based out in the wilderness instead of infesting the cities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T19:24:49-07:00","id":1198210,"title":"","content":"While the World of Darkness is not our world, it should be recognizably enough like it that someone ignorant of the supernatural should see their world more or less like we do ours. Setting elements that change the world so much that this perspective is not feasible creates problems. Either the ST has to significantly depart from expectations (which creates its own problems) or ends up excising them from the world. Unfortunately this is an issue that crops up all the time in the World of Darkness. STs really need to tone things down, remove certain things, or spend a lot of time thinking how to incorporate it into the setting.<br /> <br /> Red Talons as presented tends to fall in this category which is a shame.<br /> <br /> I think there are several things one can do to keep the feel of the Red Talons while not breaking the setting.<br /> <br /> 1) The Red Talon camps really need to be revised. How they are presented in canon should be how the OTHER tribes interpret the Red Talon camps, but it's not how the Red Talons actually are.<ul><li>The &quot;anti-extinction faction&quot;/Whelp's Compromise are basically Red Talons going on rumspringa. Almost all Red Talons go through this, and the tribe finds it is important so that the tribe learn about other Garou and mankind. Regardless of how hostile or curious the individual Red Talons are about humanity, they go through it as a learning experience and while on it, are very good about obeying the rules of other tribes.</li> <li>The Warders of the Land are those Red Talons responsible for keeping mankind out of Red Talon territories. They sometimes kill people, but they also know that killing people brings more people. They are very good at covering up killings, and having alternative means to drive people away so they don't want to enter those lands. Their tactics work well in the deep wilderness with very little people and civilization comfort, but not so well where people are plentiful.</li> <li>The Lodge of the Predator Kings is a mystic society in communion with the spirits of extinct animals, and they are preparing for the Apocalypse when the war against humanity will happen. The Talons aren't stupid enough to think the war should be fought now. It is a millenialist movement within the tribe</li> <li>The Dying Cubs are a secret society the rest of the tribe consider to be Wyrm ridden or at least Litany breakers; if you want Red Talons as the enemy this is what you use.</li> </ul>2) Red Talons choose to live far - very far - from humanity - generally the unpopulated wilderness areas of northern North America and Siberia. They should not appear in most chronicles with the exception of rare NPCs who visit other septs for the purpose of learning about the other tribes and learning about humans. This is to allow the ST an opportunity for Red Talon PCs, and allow other PCs to interact with Red Talon NPCs. In addition, a small number of packs might also be sent on specific missions on behalf of the tribe. These missions might last a long time, even decades, especially if they are intelligence gathering in nature. This is to give STs a means to have an entire pack of Red Talons as plot devices or antagonists if needed.<br /> <br /> 3) The proper portrayal of the Talons should be that of a proud, but doomed people. Their ways were fine for ten thousand years, but the last two thousand years have been very bad for them, and it is only getting worse. That should be the focus when portraying them, not genocidal instincts.<br /> <br /> 4) Talons believe humans are inherently spiritually polluting and therefore try to minimize contact as much as possible. They don't go out of their way to kill (and especially not eat) humans because that exposes them to Wyrm taint. Talons believe in spiritual purity and do everything possible to minimize such taboos. The rumspringa period is an exception, and any individuals or packs sent out in the wider world outside of that have access a skilled ritualist who can perform the Rite of Cleansing.<br /> <br /> 5) The Red Talons are actually looking forward to the Apocalypse, not because they want the Wyrm to win, but the opposite. They believe the Garou will win, and by winning they'll finally end the threat of humanity forever. They believe the world, and the current society of Garou, is corrupt and unjust. The other tribes have failed, especially their so-called leaders the Silver Fangs. But every other tribe is almost as bad except for perhaps the Wendigo and the lupus of a few others. They believe Gaia will not allow this, and that the status quo will end by a destructive force - most likely the beginning stages of the Apocalypse. That is when, finally, the Red Talons will assume de facto leadership of the Nation because they alone have kept the uncorrupted ways and can lead the Nation to victory. Because of this, the Talons are careful not to antagonize the rest of the Nation too much. They need to keep relations good enough so that they are trusted enough so they can rally the survivors.<br /> <br /> I combine the above with other elements gleamed from actual griffin mythology and legend to round out the tribe and make them more playable while keeping their essentials. I talked about that more on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/912624-heretical-thoughts-on-griffin-and-the-red-talons\">a thread located here</a>.<br /> <br /> The Red Talons have struck me for some reason, but I haven't liked how they've been developed. So this is what I've done over many years to fashion them into something I think fits better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T20:33:08-07:00","id":1198230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1057224-what-would-you-change-in-the-w-ta-setting?p=1198210#post1198210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the World of Darkness is not our world, it should be recognizably enough like it that someone ig